der (+ Christmas/NY) and mid-late July lavender — two crests","shoulder":"Late Nov-mid Dec + Mar-early Apr (spring powder); late Jun + early Aug (shoulder lavender)","green":"May-early Jun + late Sep-Oct/Nov (lifts shut, flowers gone; lowest rates)","booking_lead":"NY + Jan-Feb powder + ski-in/out apts 4-9 mo; peak-lavender July stays 3-6 mo; shoulder 1-3 mo","off_season_specials":"Spring-powder value (Mar-Apr); early-autumn onsen + wine/cheese + Tokachidake hiking; Heso Matsuri weekend","event_peaks":"NY + Feb powder (Dec-Apr ski), Hokkai Heso Matsuri 28-29 Jul, lavender peak mid-late Jul, autumn colour Sep-Oct","campaign_start":"Next winter powder + ski-in/out beds by summer; lavender July stays from prior autumn/winter; spring-powder from Jan"},"jewels":[{"name":"Dry-powder days on the Kitanomine gondola side","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~JPY 8,000/day lift (approx)","timing":"ski ~late Nov-early May; peak Jan-Feb","commission_path":"school/operator 10-15%","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Kitanomine''s 16 trails and gondola open the tree-lined, north-facing terrain where Furano''s light snow sits best","si":"ski","blurb":"Kitanomine''s 16 trails and gondola open the tree-lined, north-facing terrain where Furano''s light snow sits best","when":"ski ~late Nov-early May; peak Jan-Feb","commission":"school/operator 10-15%"},{"name":"Top-to-bottom on the Furano Zone ropeway — 829 m vertical","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~JPY 8,000/day (approx)","timing":"Deep winter Jan-Feb powder  and mid-late July lavender — two crests","commission_path":"operator 10-15%","draw_rank":2,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the fast ropeway lifts you to the summit for the resort''s longest, most sustained descents over an 829 m vertical","si":"ski","blurb":"the fast ropeway lifts you to the summit for the resort''s longest, most sustained descents over an 829 m ver