  ('zao-onsen-japan', '08A', 'Zao Onsen', 'Japan', 'Ski among the snow monsters, then soak in 1,900-year-old', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Tōhoku', '{"ski","adventure","wildlife","wellness","culture","romance","culinary","family"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["1,900-year sulphur onsen town + ski resort in Yamagata/Tohoku, ~2.5 hr from Tokyo via Yamagata Shinkansen + ~40 min bus","Signature: the juhyo ''snow monsters'' (Maries'' fir + rime ice) at Juhyogen/Jizo Sancho, best Jan-Feb (peak Feb); night Juhyo Light-up + Nightcruiser snowcat tours","Terrain: base 780 m to Jizo Sancho 1,661 m, vertical 881 m; ~50 km slopes / 57 courses (28 beg/19 int/10 adv); ~41 lifts incl 4 gondola/ropeway (skiresort.info: 50 km/35 lifts) - verify; signature run ~9 km","Strongly acidic sulphur springs (pH ~1, among Japan''s most acidic); 3 public bathhouses + 4 footbaths + ~5 day-use; Dai-Rotenburo open-air bath CLOSED in winter (~Dec-Mar/Apr)","Season early Dec-early May; main-season adult 1-day ~JPY 8,500; night skiing Uenodai 17:00-21:00 daily 20 Dec-1 Mar; Zao Ropeway to Jizo Sancho JPY 2,200 one-way / 4,400 RT","Traditional/domestic; top stays are Takamiya heritage ryokan (Miyamaso 300+ yrs, private open-air onsen) + Rurikura; NO international ultra flag (nearest ultra = Ginzan Onsen ~90 min)","Zao Snow Monster Festival 27 Dec 2025-23 Feb 2026; Torch Skiing + Winter HANABI fireworks 7 Feb 2026","VOLCANIC: Mt Zao (Okama crater) is an active JMA-monitored volcano on the summit ridge AWAY from ski runs; check live JMA alert level before summit/crater; NO dedicated JAN Tohoku avalanche bulletin"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police / 119 fire + ambulance / #7119 medical advice; ambulance dispatch free; English via third-party interpreter","hospital":"Yamagata University Hospital (Yamagata City, ~40 min, ER; after-hours 023-635-5100) via 119; confirm trauma designation/evac locally","advisory_level":"L1","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"SERIOUS AVALANCHE COUNTRY, NO dedicated JAN Tohoku bulletin: rely on local/resort-posted conditions + JAN (nadare.jp) + JMA forecasts; backcountry guided-only via Atomi Gate, beacon/probe/shovel mandatory; tree-well/deep-snow immersion suffocation risk (never ski trees alone); severe cold/wind/whiteout up top. VOLCANO: Mt Zao/Okama active (JMA-monitored, phreatic-eruption capable) on summit ridge away from runs - check live JMA alert level before summit/crater; do not touch juhyo or enter fenced zones"},"timing":{"peak":"Deep winter (Christmas/NY + Jan-Feb juhyo/snow-monster season + Lunar New Year); strong domestic + Taiwan/Asia inbound; busiest, highest rates","shoulder":"Early Dec (discounts to ~19 Dec) + Mar-early May (spring skiing, discounts from 1 Apr)","green":"Late spring-autumn: Okama crater, Zao Echo Line, hiking, foliage; Dai-Rotenburo open-air bath reopens (lowest rates)","booking_lead":"Juhyo-season ryokan (Jan-Feb weekends + light-up nights) 3-6+ mo; best Takamiya ryokan over NY/Lunar NY longer; spring/green 1-3 mo (inferred; verify)","off_season_specials":"Spring skiing (Mar-Apr discounts); green-season Okama/foliage touring; year-round onsen wellness","event_peaks":"Juhyo Light-up nights (Fri-Sun late Dec-late Feb), Torch Skiing + Winter HANABI (7 Feb 2026), Christmas/NY, Lunar New Year","campaign_start":"Juhyo season + light-up nights + best ryokan by prior summer/autumn (3-6+ mo); spring skiing from Jan; green-season Okama/foliage from late winter"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ski the ~9 km run through the snow monsters","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~JPY 8,500/day (approx)","timing":"juhyo heart Jan-Feb","commission_path":"within package","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Zao''s signature top-to-bottom descent threads ~9 km from Jizo Sancho down through the juhyo fields to the base","si":"ski","blurb":"Zao''s signature top-to-bottom descent threads ~9 km from Jizo Sancho down through the juhyo fields to the base","when":"juhyo heart Jan-Feb","commission":"within package"},{"name":"Ride the ropeway to the monster fields","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~JPY 2,200 one-way / 4,400 RT (approx)","timing":"juhyo season Dec-Mar","commission_path":"reseller/within package","draw_rank":2,"hook":"the ropeway climbs Zao Sanroku → Juhyo Kogen → Jizo Sancho; winter fares to Jizo Sancho run ¥2,200 one-way / ¥4,400 round-trip adult","si":"ski","blurb":"the ropeway climbs Zao Sanroku → Juhyo Kogen → Jizo Sancho; winter fares to Jizo Sancho run ¥2,200 one-way / ¥4,400 round-trip adult","when":"juhyo season Dec-Mar","commission":"reseller/within package"},{"name":"First tracks in dry Zao powder","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"~JPY 8,500/day (approx)","timing":"powder heart Jan-Feb; mornings","commission_path":"within package","draw_rank":3,"hook":"cold, exposed and high, Zao''s upper mountain holds dry, light snow for early-lift powder laps beneath the frozen firs","si":"ski","blurb":"cold, exposed and high, Zao''s upper mountain holds dry, light snow for early-lift powder laps beneath the frozen firs","when":"powder heart Jan-Feb; mornings","commission":"within package"},{"name":"Night skiing at Uenodai","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"night ticket (approx; verify)","timing":"20 Dec-1 Mar","commission_path":"within package","draw_rank":4,"hook":"evening laps on the Uenodai slope below the illuminated upper mountain — a low-cost only-here night on the snow","si":"ski","blurb":"evening laps on the Uenodai slope below the illuminated upper mountain — a low-cost only-here night on the snow","when":"20 Dec-1 Mar","commission":"within package"},{"name":"Spring skiing on discounted late-season passes","si_tag":"Winter/Ski","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_band":"discounted spring (approx; verify)","timing":"Apr-early May","commission_path":"w