s and stalactites","bookable_category":"liveaboard berth","commission_path":"fleet-direct","source":"https://palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau/","timing":"Nov-May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"a cavern with air chambers and stalactites","when":"Nov-May","commission":"fleet-direct"},{"name":"German Channel manta route (Dec-Mar)","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"the winter manta-aggregation week","bookable_category":"liveaboard week","commission_path":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer)","source":"https://palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau/","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"the winter manta-aggregation week","commission":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer)"},{"name":"Blue Corner + Blue Holes + Ngemelis wall route","si_tag":"liveaboard","status":"live","tier":"premier","hook":"the classic marquee-wall liveaboard arc","bookable_category":"liveaboard week","commission_path":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer)","source":"https://palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau/","timing":"Nov-May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","blurb":"the classic marquee-wall liveaboard arc","when":"Nov-May","commission":"fleet-direct (Aggressor/Explorer)"},{"name":"Peleliu WWII battlefield + Rock Islands (UNESCO)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the WWII island ashore and the Rock Islands Southern Lagoon seascape","bookable_category":"DMC / liveaboard-included excursion","commission_path":"DMC / excursion pass-through","source":"https://palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau/","timing":"Nov-May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"the WWII island ashore and the Rock Islands Southern Lagoon seascape","when":"Nov-May","commission":"DMC / excursion pass-through"},{"name":"Jellyfish Lake (Ongeim''l Tketau)","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"the permit-based golden-jellyfish lake; snorkel-only, scuba prohibited","bookable_category":"permit / DMC","commission_path":"permit / DMC pass-through","source":"https://palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau/","timing":"Nov-May","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"the permit-based golden-jellyfish lake; snorkel-only, scuba prohibited","when":"Nov-May","commission":"permit / DMC pass-through"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the current advisory for Palau, and how do I dive it responsibly?","a":"The U.S. State Department places Palau at Level 1 - Exercise Normal Precautions, and the UK FCDO issues no advice against travel, describing crime levels as low. Both note practical hazards rather than restrictions: unexploded WWII ordnance (found mainly on Peleliu - stay on marked paths and do not touch ordnance), diving hazards, and tropical cyclones, with an overnight curfew in Koror. The two governments agree on a Level 1 posture. Carry DAN membership plus dive-accident insurance with strong evacuation cover - the Palau Siren operator stresses that insurance covering emergency evacuation, chamber treatment and medical costs is a must - and observe an 18-24 hour no-fly window after diving.","source":"travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/palau-travel-advisory.html + gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palau/safety-and-security + masterliveaboards.com/faq/palau (all accessed 2026-08-09)","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is there a recompression chamber, and how remote is care?","a":"Palau has one hyperbaric facility for divers - a recompression chamber at Belau National Hospital in Koror. Hospital sources describe it as operational in 2026 with a trained barotrauma team, but availability can vary, so confirm its status with your dive operator or DAN before the trip. Because the archipelago is dispersed, serious cases can require evacuation by speedboat from the vessel and, in some cases, onward air evacuation to Manila - which is why evacuation-grade dive insurance matters here.","source":"masterliveaboards.com/faq/palau (accessed 2026-08-09)","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When is the best time to dive Palau, and when do the mantas aggregate?","a":"The peak liveaboard season is November through May, with warm water (28-30C) year-round. For mantas at German Channel, the winter months are best - January and February can bring dozens of mantas to the cleaning station.","source":"masterliveaboards.com/faq/palau + palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau","si_tag":"planning"},{"q":"Which sites define a Palau liveaboard week?","a":"Blue Corner (the reef-hook shark drift), German Channel (mantas), Ulong Channel (a drift past giant clams and lettuce coral), the Blue Holes cavern, the Peleliu walls, Siaes Tunnel and New Drop-Off - plus the snorkel-only Jellyfish Lake as a non-dive highlight.","source":"palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"What conditions and certification should I plan for?","a":"Blue Corner, Peleliu Express and the channel dives are strong-current drift dives where a reef hook and good buoyancy are essential, best suited to experienced divers; sheltered reefs, Chandelier Cave and the lake suit a wider range with a guide. Nitrox is standard on liveaboards for the multi-day profile. Dive within your certification and the operator briefing.","source":"palaudiveadventures.com/dive-palau","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How far ahead do Palau liveaboards book?","a":"The November-May peak on the marquee vessels fills earliest, with the January-February manta weeks in most demand; hold roughly 6-12 months out for peak windows and preferred boats, nearer term for the shoulder. Confirm per-vessel lead times with the operator.","source":"masterliveaboards.com/faq/palau","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Palau Liveaboard Diving: Blue Corner, Mantas & Season","meta_description":"The Palau liveaboard sea - Blue Corner''s reef-hook shark drift, the German Channel mantas, Blue Holes and the Peleliu walls, the Nov-May season, operators and safety.","slug":"palau-micronesia","primary_keyword":"Palau liveaboard diving","long_tail":["Blue Corner Palau","German Channel manta","Palau dive season","Peleliu wall dive","Palau liveaboard operators"],"search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Palau diving","Blue Corner","German Channel manta"],"hreflang":["en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-08-09"},"booking":{"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","level":"L1 (Exercise Normal Precautions)","codes":["L1"],"consent_flow":false,"note":"US State Dept Level 1 (Exercise Normal Precautions), accessed 2026-08-09 (travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/.../palau-travel-advisory.html). FCDO cross-check (gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/palau/safety-and-security, accessed 2026-08-09): no advice against travel; crime levels low; terrorism cannot be ruled out but no recent history. Both flag unexploded WWII ordnance (mainly Peleliu) + diving/tropical-cyclone hazards. Both at L1 posture."},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-09","hits":4,"misses":18,"disregarded":3,"note":"Liveaboard-diving scope; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","name":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private full-boat charter (Palau Aggressor II or Palau Siren) across the marquee walls + German Channel manta weeks + Rock Islands/Peleliu land layer + Koror pre/post","why_ultra":"the Palau ultra pull is a private full-boat charter pairing the marquee walls, the manta channel and the WWII/Rock Islands layer ashore","earning":"held Aggressor/Explorer reseller lines; verify Master/charter terms","virtuoso_value_add":"verify - not documented","mor":"commission-on-net; no net-rate resale markup","source":"handoff/LIVEABOARD-OPERATOR-GRID-2026-08-09.md"}],"source_verified":"2026-08-09","hero":{"query":"Palau, Palau"},"geo":{"lat":7.34,"lng":134.48}}'::jsonb, 3),
  ('machu-picchu-peru', '10S', 'Machu Picchu', 'Peru', '*If it''s a lost city in the clouds, reached', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Cusco, Sacred Valley & Machu Picchu', '{"expedition","romance","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Machu Picchu citadel sits at 2,430 m; Cusco gateway at ~3,400 m — altitude, not crime, is the headline planning constraint.","Entry is by timed circuit ticket only (no free roaming); daily cap 4,500 standard / 5,600 high season (Jun 19–Nov 2).","Classic Inca Trail is guided-mandatory, capped at 500 permits/day (~200 hikers), sells out 4–7 months ahead, and closes every February.","Cusco / Sacred Valley / Inca Trail / Machu Picchu are State-Dept-named as NOT in any higher-risk advisory area — the strongest clean-zone in South America.","Rail from Ollantaytambo (~1h45m) via PeruRail/Inca Rail; the Belmond Hiram Bingham is the luxury tier and bundles citadel entry, bus and guide."],"safety":{"emergency":"105","emergency_ambulance":"117","tourist_line":"iPerú / Policía de Turismo","hospital":"Cusco private clinics for routine + altitude care; serious cases evac to Lima (Clínica Anglo Americana / Ricardo Palma); Aguas Calientes + trail remote","advisory_level":"L2","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow_required":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Cusco (CUZ) via Lima (LIM); then rail Ollantaytambo → Aguas Calientes; shuttle bus to the gate","altitude_m":{"cusco":3400,"citadel":2430,"sacred_valley_base":2800,"dead_womans_pass":4215,"salkantay_pass":4650,"rainbow_mountain":5000},"altitude_note":"Acute mountain sickness (soroche) is the primary health risk; acclimatize in the lower Sacred Valley first, ascend gradually, coca tea","water":"bottled/purified only","malaria":"none at altitude (Cusco/Sacred Valley/Machu Picchu); malaria risk is in the low-elevation Amazon"},"timing":{"peak":"June–August (dry season; Jun–Jul apex; citadel cap 5,600 Jun 19–Nov 2)","inflection_curve_start":"early December (prior year); tickets release ~Nov 17","fire_date":"2026-11-24","shoulder":"April–May & September–October","green":"November–March (lush/wet; February = Inca Trail closed)","booking_lead":"Inca Trail 4–7 months for peak (6–7 Jun–Jul); citadel timed tickets weeks–months; marquee hotels + Hiram Bingham as early as the permit","off_season":"Nov–Mar green-season Salkantay/Lares + Vistadome rail packages","event_peaks":["Inti Raymi — Festival of the Sun, Cusco, June 24"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Dawn entry via the Sun Gate (Inti Punku)","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Inca Trail finishers walk in at first light — the most cinematic arrival at the citadel","bookable_category":"guided_trek_package","tier":"premier","commission_path":"direct-operator DMC via OutsideAgents/Fora","source":"https://www.ticketmachupicchu.com/hiking-guide-sun-gate/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"Inca Trail finishers walk in at first light — the most cinematic arrival at the citadel","when":"June–August","commission":"direct-operator DMC via OutsideAgents/Fora"},{"name":"Huayna Picchu","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"The iconic peak behind the postcard — straight-down views, 400 permits/day","bookable_category":"circuit_ticket_addon","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC/tour add-on (ticket non-commissionable; guiding earns)","source":"https://www.samtravelperu.com/index.php/peru-treks-machu-picchu-cuzco/huayna-picchu-mountain-availability-permits-information-machupicchu-mt-sun-gate-inka-bidge","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"The iconic peak behind the postcard — straight-down views, 400 permits/day","when":"June–August","commission":"DMC/tour add-on (ticket non-commissionable; guiding earns)"},{"name":"Machu Picchu Mountain","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Higher than Huayna, less exposed — big view without the ladders","bookable_category":"circuit_ticket_addon","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC package","source":"https://adventuresmithexplorations.com/land-tours/peru/machu-picchu-hike-options-explained/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"Higher than Huayna, less exposed — big view without the ladders","when":"June–August","commission":"DMC package"},{"name":"Salkantay Trek","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Glaciers + the 4,650 m pass + snow-to-jungle; ideal green-season fill","bookable_category":"trek_package","tier":"premier","commission_path":"trek operator via OutsideAgents","source":"https://trexperienceperu.com/blog/salkantay-trek-vs-lares-trek","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"Glaciers + the 4,650 m pass + snow-to-jungle; ideal green-season fill","when":"June–August","commission":"trek operator via OutsideAgents"},{"name":"Lares Trek","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"The gentle cultural route through Quechua villages — quietest, most human","bookable_category":"trek_package","tier":"premier","commission_path":"trek operator via OutsideAgents","source":"https://nickey-travel.com/blog/lares-trek-vs-salkantay/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"The gentle cultural route through Quechua villages — quietest, most human","when":"June–August","commission":"trek operator via OutsideAgents"},{"name":"The Inca Bridge","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Short quiet cliff-edge walk to a defensive Inca bridge — low-effort secret","bookable_category":"included_in_ticket_walk","tier":"essential","commission_path":"sold inside guided day tour","source":"https://www.samtravelperu.com/index.php/peru-treks-machu-picchu-cuzco/huayna-picchu-mountain-availability-permits-information-machupicchu-mt-sun-gate-inka-bidge","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"GEA","blurb":"Short quiet cliff-edge walk to a defensive Inca bridge — low-effort secret","when":"year-round","commission":"sold inside guided day tour"},{"name":"Putucusi","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Free, wild, ladder-climbed view across at the citadel — experienced hikers only","bookable_category":"free_unguided","tier":"essential","commission_path":"none (content/SEO value only)","source":"https://www.ticketmachupicchu.com/alternatives-see-machu-picchu-from-above/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"Free, wild, ladder-climbed view across at the citadel — experienced hikers only","when":"June–August","commission":"none (content/SEO value only)"},{"name":"Belmond Hiram Bingham train","si_tag":"Romance","status":"live","hook":"Polished-brass luxe rail; bundles entry + bus + guide + gourmet dining","bookable_category":"luxury_rail","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"Belmond/PeruRail via Fora/Virtuoso","source":"https://www.belmond.com/trains/south-america/peru/belmond-hiram-bingham/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Polished-brass luxe rail; bundles entry + bus + guide + gourmet dining","when":"June–August","commission":"Belmond/PeruRail via Fora/Virtuoso"},{"name":"Vistadome / 360 scenic trains","si_tag":"Romance","status":"live","hook":"Glass-roof panoramic cars — accessible romance below Hiram Bingham","bookable_category":"scenic_rail","tier":"premier","commission_path":"PeruRail/Inca Rail affiliate + DMC bundle","source":"https://heatherjasper.com/peru-blogs-travel-tips/machu-picchu-train","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Glass-roof panoramic cars — accessible romance below Hiram Bingham","when":"June–August","commission":"PeruRail/Inca Rail affiliate + DMC bundle"},{"name":"Aguas Calientes hot springs","si_tag":"Romance","status":"live","hook":"The town''s namesake thermal baths — a soak to unknot the legs post-trek","bookable_category":"entry_addon","tier":"essential","commission_path":"affiliate/entry add-on","source":"https://www.perurail.com/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"The town''s namesake thermal baths — a soak to unknot the legs post-trek","when":"June–August","commission":"affiliate/entry add-on"},{"name":"Inti Raymi — Festival of the Sun (Cusco, Jun 24)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Reconstructed Inca solstice ceremony at Sacsayhuamán — bucket-list cultural anchor","bookable_category":"festival_package","tier":"premier","commission_path":"Cusco DMC festival package via OutsideAgents/Fora","source":"https://www.cuscoperu.com/en/festivities-events/may-june/inti-raymi/","timing":"June–August","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Reconstructed Inca solstice ceremony at Sacsayhuamán — bucket-list cultural anchor","when":"June–August","commission":"Cusco DMC festival package via OutsideAgents/Fora"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Machu Picchu safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Peru carries a US State Dept Level 2 \"Exercise Increased Caution,\" but the advisory states verbatim that Cusco, the Sacred Valley, the Inca Trail and Machu Picchu \"are not located in the affected area.\" The Level 4 zones (Colombia border in Loreto; the VRAEM) are geographically separate from the whole tourist corridor.","source":"travel.state.gov, reissued 2025-05-16","si_tag":""},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Machu Picchu?","a":"Altitude, not crime. Cusco sits at ~3,400 m and acute mountain sickness (*soroche*) is the primary health risk — headache, nausea, breathlessness. Acclimatize in the lower Sacred Valley (~2,800 m) before Cusco or any trek, ascend gradually, and rest day one; the citadel itself (2,430 m) is lower, so many feel better there.","source":"alpacaexpeditions.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":""},{"q":"How hard is the Inca Trail, and do I need a guide?","a":"You cannot legally hike the classic trail without a licensed guide, and it is demanding, not casual. Only 500 permits are issued per day (~200 hikers), the trail closes every February, and the Day-2 crux is Dead Woman''s Pass at 4,215 m — a ~1,200 m ascent where oxygen is ~60% of sea level. Book 4–7 months ahead for peak.","source":"incatrail.org / machupicchusoul.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the Huayna Picchu climb dangerous?","a":"It''s exposed but managed — bookable for the sure-footed. Huayna Picchu is a ~2-hour climb capped at 400 permits/day, with big drop-offs, narrow original Inca stairs and cable-assisted sections; it is not for those uneasy with heights. Machu Picchu Mountain is the longer, higher, less-exposed alternative.","source":"samtravelperu.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the Belmond Hiram Bingham worth it for a honeymoon?","a":"For a marquee honeymoon, yes — it removes the ticket-scramble. The Hiram Bingham bundles citadel entry, bus and guide into a ~1h45m polished-brass rail run, and pairs with the Sanctuary Lodge, the only hotel at the gate (first in at dawn, last out at dusk). Hold both as early as the trek permit.","source":"belmond.com / thesouthamericaspecialists.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Machu Picchu?","a":"May–October (dry season) is best and June–August is clearest — cloudless mornings — because the wet season (Nov–March) is lusher but rainier and February closes the Inca Trail entirely. The daily citadel cap also rises to 5,600 for the Jun 19–Nov 2 high-season block, so book early.","source":"salkantaytrekking.com / bushop.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","meta_title":"Machu Picchu, Peru — When to Go, Inca Trail Permits, Tickets & Where to Stay (2026)","search_language":"es-PE","local_keywords":["Machu Picchu entradas","Camino Inca permisos","cómo llegar a Machu Picchu","boletos Machu Picchu 2026 circuitos","mal de altura Cusco soroche","tren a Machu Picchu PeruRail","Salkantay o Lares","Huayna Picchu entradas","Valle Sagrado aclimatación","Inti Raymi Cusco 24 de junio"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Sanctuary Lodge, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"Only hotel adjacent to the citadel gate — first in at dawn, last out at dusk","earning":"Belmond commission via Fora/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Bellini-Club perks: breakfast, credit, upgrades, priority dawn access","mor":"Hotel/DMC direct or Fora","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Inkaterra Machu Picchu Pueblo Hotel","why_ultra":"Relais & Châteaux, 85 rooms, private 5-ha cloud-forest reserve at 2,450 m","earning":"R&C/Inkaterra commission via Fora/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Nature/conservation programming + R&C amenities","mor":"Hotel/DMC direct or Fora","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Sumaq Machu Picchu Hotel","why_ultra":"Culinary-forward luxury: tasting menus, pisco/cooking workshops, Andean ceremonies","earning":"Hotel commission via Fora/OutsideAgents","virtuoso_value_add":"Pre-loaded chef + cultural experiences","mor":"Hotel/DMC direct or Fora","tier":"premier–luxury"},{"name":"Belmond Hiram Bingham (rail)","why_ultra":"World''s most storied luxury train to the Wonder; bundles entry + bus + guide + dining","earning":"Belmond/PeruRail commission via Fora/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Bundled citadel access removes the ticket-scramble","mor":"Belmond/PeruRail","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Machu Picchu, Peru"},"geo":{"lat":-13.1631,"lng":-72.545}}'::jsonb, 0),
  ('patagonia-chile-argentina', '10S', 'Patagonia', 'Chile / Argentina', 'Granite spires and turquoise lakes', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', null, '{}', '{}', '{}', null, null, null, 1),
  ('cartagena-colombia', '10S', 'Cartagena & Colombia''s Caribbean Coast', 'Colombia', 'Walled colonial casas and Caribbean nights **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Colombia''s Caribbean Coast', '{"romance","tropical","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Cartagena''s Ciudad Amurallada (walled old city + fortifications) is the anchor; Castillo San Felipe is the largest Spanish fort in South America; most visitors need 3–4 days.","Islas del Rosario + Barú (Playa Blanca) — ~1hr speedboat to Corales del Rosario National Park, reef snorkel, beach lunch.","Getsemaní — best street art on the coast + Plaza de la Trinidad salsa nights, just outside the walls.","Santa Marta + Tayrona NP protect 150 km² where the Sierra Nevada meets the sea; Cabo San Juan is the iconic cove.","Barranquilla Carnival — UNESCO Intangible Heritage, largest carnival outside Brazil; 2026 dates 14–17 February."],"safety":{"emergency":"123","hospital":"Cartagena private hospitals (stabilization); serious cases route to Bogotá or US medical evacuation","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"risk_code_meanings":{"C":"Crime — violent crime (murder, assault, robbery), drugging (scopolamine), extortion, express kidnapping occur throughout Colombia incl. cities","T":"Terrorism — attacks possible with little/no warning; car bombs, grenades, IEDs, drones","U":"Unrest — demonstrations can shut roads and turn violent","K":"Kidnapping or Hostage-Taking — kidnapping-for-ransom reported","N":"Natural Disaster — volcano, earthquake, landslide"},"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"cartagena_in_named_danger":false,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Colombia (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"CTG (Rafael Núñez Intl) — direct international incl. Miami (AA, Avianca) and New York JFK (JetBlue year-round, Avianca seasonal)","water":"bottled","vaccinations":"yellow fever recommended for Tayrona/jungle/Sierra Nevada; dengue present on coast; check CDC","scopolamine_caution":"''devil''s breath''/burundanga drugging — colourless/tasteless; never accept drinks/food/tabs from strangers; dating-app method documented in Cartagena"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec–Mar/Apr (dry); true peak mid-Dec → mid/late-Jan","inflection_curve_start":"early December","fire_date":"mid-to-late November (peak); ~late-January (Barranquilla Carnival)","event_peaks":[{"event":"Barranquilla Carnival","dates_2026":"14–17 February","note":"UNESCO; largest carnival outside Brazil; Barranquilla rooms sell out/price hard"},{"event":"Independence Day (Cartagena)","dates":"November 11","note":"coastal rates +30–40% Nov 9–12"},{"event":"Christmas–New Year","dates":"Dec 20–31","note":"maximum annual congestion"}],"off_season_fill":"Aug–Nov (rates ~half of peak); Jul–Aug veranillo del Niño = best weather-to-cost"},"jewels":[{"name":"Walled Old City + rampart sunset (Café del Mar)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","commission_path":"hotel + city-tour affiliate; wedding via DMC/villa","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/top-things-to-do-in-cartagena-colombia","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"cobbled lanes, Plaza Santo Domingo, and a sunset walk on the coral-stone ramparts","si":"romance","blurb":"cobbled lanes, Plaza Santo Domingo, and a sunset walk on the coral-stone ramparts","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"hotel + city-tour affiliate; wedding via DMC/villa"},{"name":"Walled-city colonial-mansion buyout wedding","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","commission_path":"MoR villa + wedding DMC ~10–20% land","source":"https://cartagenadreams.com/explore-cartagena/old-city/unesco-walled-city-colonial-mansion-rental-groups-your-complete-guide-to-cartagena/","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"take over a restored 17th–18th-c. casa for ceremony + dinners + party","si":"romance","blurb":"take over a restored 17th–18th-c. casa for ceremony + dinners + party","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"MoR villa + wedding DMC ~10–20% land"},{"name":"Rosario private-island wedding (yacht/speedboat)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"DMC + island villa MoR","source":"https://two.travel/planning-your-wedding-in-cartagena-colombia/","si":"romance","commission":"DMC + island villa MoR"},{"name":"Islas del Rosario + Barú (Playa Blanca)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"GetYourGuide/Viator affiliate; island villa MoR","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/cartagena-l362/cartagena-rosario-islands-and-playa-blanca-excursion-with-snorkeling-or-aquarium-t934710/","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"reef snorkel in Corales del Rosario NP, beach-club lunch, hammocks on Playa Blanca","si":"tropical","blurb":"reef snorkel in Corales del Rosario NP, beach-club lunch, hammocks on Playa Blanca","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"GetYourGuide/Viator affiliate; island villa MoR"},{"name":"Cabo San Juan, Tayrona NP","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Santa Marta DMC + park fee pass-through","source":"https://mytriptocolombia.com/visit-parc-tayrona/","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"Santa Marta DMC + park fee pass-through"},{"name":"Palomino river-tube + beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"coast DMC + boutique-lodge affiliate","source":"https://smallgirlbigbackpack.com/how-to-get-to-tayrona-national-park/","si":"tropical","commission":"coast DMC + boutique-lodge affiliate"},{"name":"Getsemaní (street art, Plaza de la Trinidad, Café Havana)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"walking-tour affiliate + boutique lodging","source":"https://www.cartagenaexplorer.com/getsemani-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"walking-tour affiliate + boutique lodging"},{"name":"Castillo San Felipe de Barajas","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"city-tour affiliate","source":"https://mycartagenatrip.com/things-to-do-in-cartagena/","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the largest Spanish fort in South America, on a hill over the city","si":"culture","blurb":"the largest Spanish fort in South America, on a hill over the city","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"city-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Minca (coffee/cloud forest, Sierra Nevada)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Santa Marta DMC + eco-lodge affiliate","source":"https://mytriptocolombia.com/visit-parc-tayrona/","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"Santa Marta DMC + eco-lodge affiliate"},{"name":"Ciudad Perdida (Teyuna) 4-day trek","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","commission_path":"licensed-operator DMC (mandatory)","source":"https://www.kimkim.com/c/the-lost-city-tayrona-park-adventure-10-days","hook":"4-day guided-only trek to pre-Columbian ruins in the Sierra Nevada","si":"culture","blurb":"4-day guided-only trek to pre-Columbian ruins in the Sierra Nevada","commission":"licensed-operator DMC (mandatory)"},{"name":"Barranquilla Carnival","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","commission_path":"event DMC + Barranquilla hotel affiliate (fire ~late-Jan)","source":"https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/carnival-of-barranquilla-00051","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"UNESCO Masterpiece of Intangible Heritage, largest carnival outside Brazil; 2026 dates 14–17 Feb","si":"culture","blurb":"UNESCO Masterpiece of Intangible Heritage, largest carnival outside Brazil; 2026 dates 14–17 Feb","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"event DMC + Barranquilla hotel affiliate (fire ~late-Jan)"},{"name":"Mompox (UNESCO colonial river town)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","commission_path":"specialist heritage DMC + boutique lodging","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barranquilla_Carnival","timing":"Dec–Mar/Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec–Mar/Apr","commission":"specialist heritage DMC + boutique lodging"}],"faq":[{"q":"How much does a walled-city wedding in Cartagena cost?","a":"A private-villa wedding for 40–60 guests starts around USD $40,000, including a 2–3-night buyout of a restored colonial casa with pool, rooftop, chef, butler and security. Cartagena''s wedding DMCs assemble venue, villa, catering and logistics as the agent-of-record (~10–20% land).","source":"cartagenadreams.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"How do you get to the Rosario Islands and Playa Blanca from Cartagena?","a":"By speedboat — about 1 hour offshore to the Corales del Rosario y San Bernardo National Park for reef snorkeling and a beach-club lunch on Playa Blanca (Barú). Book a licensed day-tour; the ~1-hr open-water return chops up in the windy Dec–Apr season, so tours often head back earlier.","source":"tomplanmytrip.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What are the must-do sights in Cartagena?","a":"The walled Ciudad Amurallada is the anchor — most visitors need 3–4 days — with Castillo San Felipe de Barajas, the largest Spanish fort in South America, and Getsemaní''s street art and Plaza de la Trinidad salsa nights just outside the walls.","source":"mycartagenatrip.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Cartagena safe to visit right now?","a":"Colombia is at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (issued 2026-03-31, codes C·T·U·K·N), but Cartagena (Bolívar) and the Caribbean coast are NOT in the named Level-4 Do-Not-Travel areas — those are Arauca, Cauca (excl. Popayán), Valle del Cauca (excl. Cali), Norte de Santander, and within ~10 km of the Venezuela border. Cartagena has direct international air (CTG).","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cartagena?","a":"Scopolamine (\"devil''s breath\") drugging is the headline traveler risk — colourless and tasteless, slipped into drinks or offered items to incapacitate and rob. The US Embassy singled out Cartagena (with Medellín and Bogotá) as a hotspot, often via dating apps. Never accept drinks, food or tabs from strangers, and travel during daylight.","source":"financecolombia.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is hiking and swimming in Tayrona National Park safe?","a":"Mostly, with discipline: it''s a hot 2-hour jungle trek to Cabo San Juan (enter by ~08:00 before the midday heat), but some beaches have strong riptides and are designated no-swim — obey the signage. Carry water, insect protection and yellow-fever cover. The separate 4-day Ciudad Perdida trek is licensed-guide-only.","source":"mytriptocolombia.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cartagena & Colombia''s Caribbean Coast — Walled-City Weddings, Rosario Islands & Tayrona | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CO","long_tail_en":["things to do in Cartagena Colombia","Cartagena walled city weddings","Rosario Islands day trip from Cartagena","Tayrona National Park Cabo San Juan guide","is Cartagena safe 2026","Cartagena luxury colonial hotels"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Cartagena","Islas del Rosario tour","Ciudad Amurallada Cartagena","bodas Cartagena","Parque Tayrona Cabo San Juan","hoteles de lujo Cartagena"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","tropical","culture"],"ultra":[{"name":"Sofitel Legend Santa Clara","type":"17th-c. former monastery, walled city — prestige address","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa Pestagua","type":"18th-c. palace, Relais & Châteaux, Two MICHELIN Keys 2025","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa San Agustín","type":"11-key colonial mansion, Leading Hotels of the World","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hotel Charleston Santa Teresa","type":"grande-dame walled-city luxury","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury→ultra"},{"name":"Tcherassi Hotel + Spa","type":"designer boutique, restored colonial house","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Blue Apple Beach (Barú)","type":"design beach club + villa, Barú island","routing":"villa/MoR + host","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Walled-city private villas","type":"full colonial-house buyouts, chef/butler/security","routing":"MoR villa + wedding DMC","tier":"ultra"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Cartagena & Colombia''s Caribbean Coast, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":10.391,"lng":-75.4794}}'::jsonb, 2),
  ('akumal-mexico', '10S', 'Akumal', 'Mexico', 'Turtle bay, cenotes and reef **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"diveglobal","ocean","culture"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Akumal means ''place of the turtles'' in Maya; the bay''s seagrass beds feed wild green sea turtles.","A certified guide and life jacket are mandatory to enter the turtle-snorkel area.","No touching turtles (federal offense); keep 3 m distance, 2 min per turtle, biodegradable sunscreen or rashguard only.","Turtle sightings permitted 8am-5pm; sessions cap at ~55 minutes; no fins, no diving on the circuit.","Cenote and reef diving are easily reached, making Akumal a serene dive base."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Nearest trauma: Hospiten Riviera Maya, Playa del Carmen (+52 984 159 2200), ~25 min north; local clinics stabilize/transfer; major trauma to Cancún","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none in tourist Quintana Roo","yellow_fever":"none required"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry season; highest rates, biggest crowds)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off, good weather)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane/low; cheapest)","turtle_season":"green turtles graze year-round; snorkel 8am-5pm, <=55-min sessions; nesting ~May-Oct overlaps green/sargassum months","sargassum_window":"Apr-Aug (Jun-Jul peak); Akumal affected (seagrass bay, naturally weedy)","booking_window_lead_time":"peak 3-4 months (villa stock finite, book earlier); shoulder 4-6 months","holiday_event_peaks":["Christmas/New Year","Spring Break (Mar)","Semana Santa"],"fill_the_beds":"sargassum/green months lead with Yal-Ku Lagoon, cenote dives, reef dives, Tulum-ruin loops, turtle morning at opening","campaign_start_trigger":"peak campaigns open Aug-Sep; shoulder ~3-4 months out; turtle-nesting off-peak push into green season"},"jewels":[{"name":"Guided Akumal Bay turtle snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Certified-guide snorkel over seagrass to see wild green turtles — no touch, low impact.","bookable_category":"guided snorkel tour","commission_path":"Amstar 12% / affiliate; bay + guide fees pass-through","source":"https://absolute-adventure-mexico.com/snorkeling/akumal-bay-regulation-swim-with-the-turtles/","si":"ocean","blurb":"Certified-guide snorkel over seagrass to see wild green turtles — no touch, low impact.","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate; bay + guide fees pass-through"},{"name":"Yal-Ku Lagoon snorkel","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Calm brackish lagoon where cenote freshwater meets the sea, rich in fish.","bookable_category":"snorkel add-on","commission_path":"affiliate 4-8%; entry pass-through","source":"https://alohawanderers.com/puerto-aventuras-what-to-know-before-visiting-this-riviera-maya-gem/","si":"ocean","blurb":"Calm brackish lagoon where cenote freshwater meets the sea, rich in fish.","commission":"affiliate 4-8%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Akumal-area cenote cavern dive","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Guided cavern dives inland pair the turtle bay with cave country.","bookable_category":"cenote cavern dive (guide required)","commission_path":"DMC 12% / affiliate 4-8%","source":"https://alohawanderers.com/puerto-aventuras-what-to-know-before-visiting-this-riviera-maya-gem/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Guided cavern dives inland pair the turtle bay with cave country.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"DMC 12% / affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Akumal reef dive","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"Shallow near-shore reef dives with easy multi-dive days.","bookable_category":"reef dive","commission_path":"dive-operator affiliate / DMC 12%","source":"https://www.prodiveinternational.com/diving/mexico/puerto-aventuras/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Shallow near-shore reef dives with easy multi-dive days.","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator affiliate / DMC 12%"},{"name":"Tulum ruins + turtle-bay combo day","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"Cliff-top Maya ruins paired with an Akumal turtle morning.","bookable_category":"guided combo excursion","commission_path":"Amstar 12%; ruin/bay entry pass-through","source":"https://www.embracethejourneytravel.com/agent-portal/vendor-list/amstar/","si":"culture","blurb":"Cliff-top Maya ruins paired with an Akumal turtle morning.","commission":"Amstar 12%; ruin/bay entry pass-through"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Akumal safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable, no hold. Akumal sits in Quintana Roo, which carries a standard US State Dept Level 2 \"Exercise Increased Caution\" (dated 2026-05-29) — the same caution applied to most of Mexico''s resort states. The village is a calm, gated bay community; apply normal precautions and stay aware after dark.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-05-29","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Akumal?","a":"Sargassum, water, mosquitoes and hurricanes — not violent crime. 2026 is tracking a record sargassum year, with Akumal affected Apr–Aug (Jun–Jul peak) because the bay is seagrass habitat and naturally weedy by design; drink bottled/purified water only, use repellent for dengue (peak May–November, no malaria), and note hurricane season runs June–November.","source":"deeparrival.com / cdc.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is swimming with the Akumal turtles safe and ethical?","a":"Yes, when you go guided and follow the rules — this is Akumal''s signature protected activity. A certified guide and life jacket are mandatory to enter the turtle area, you must keep ≥3 m distance and ≤2 minutes per turtle, wear a rashguard or biodegradable sunscreen only, and never touch a turtle — it is a federal offense. Sessions run 8am–5pm, capped at ~55 minutes.","source":"absolute-adventure-mexico.com / fearlessfemaletravels.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Can you swim with wild sea turtles in Akumal, and when''s best?","a":"Yes — it is the whole reason to come, and green turtles graze the bay''s seagrass year-round. Go at 8am opening for the calmest water and fewest boats; snorkeling is permitted only 8am–5pm in sessions capped at ~55 minutes, always with a certified guide over the seagrass beds.","source":"absolute-adventure-mexico.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Can I dive cenotes and reef from Akumal?","a":"Yes — Akumal makes a serene dive base for both. Guided cenote cavern dives sit just inland (Cenote Azul corridor) and shallow reef dives are close to shore; cavern diving requires a certified cave/cavern guide and stays in the daylight zone. Observe no-fly of 18h single / 24h repetitive; the nearest chamber is ~25 min north in Playa del Carmen.","source":"sssnetwork.com / alohawanderers.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Akumal good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes, if you want quiet and private over resort buzz. Akumal is villa-driven — beachfront villas with private pools and chef service, plus the wider luxury tier at ~US$400–600+/night in March — and it is calmer and more purposeful than Playa or Tulum. For branded ultra, Rosewood/Banyan Tree at Mayakoba sit ~35–40 min north with an easy turtle-morning day trip.","source":"machupicchu.org / rentalescapes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Akumal, and when is it cheapest?","a":"Nov–March is the best weather window; the cheapest is the green season, June–mid-October. Peak Dec–Apr brings the best conditions and highest rates; May–June and November shoulders run ~30–40% off with thinner crowds; the green season is hot, rainy and cheapest but carries hurricane exposure (Jun–Nov).","source":"machupicchu.org / travelswithelle.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Can I visit Maya ruins from Akumal?","a":"Yes — Akumal pairs a turtle morning with cliff-top Maya ruins in a single day. Tulum''s ruins are a short drive south and Cobá is inland; a common loop is ruins at 8–10am then the turtle bay after, bookable as a guided combo excursion.","source":"embracethejourneytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Akumal Travel Guide 2026 — Swim with Sea Turtles Responsibly | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Akumal, ''place of the turtles'': guided no-touch turtle snorkeling rules, cenote & reef diving, straight 2026 sargassum, Level 2 safety and nearest dive-chamber contacts.","slug":"akumal-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["nadar con tortugas en Akumal","reglas nadar con tortugas Akumal 2026","snorkel en Akumal","buceo en cenotes Akumal","mejor época para ver tortugas en Akumal","sargazo Akumal 2026","Laguna Yal-Ku Akumal","villas frente al mar Akumal"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Akumal beachfront luxury villas","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":false,"earning":"on application / host or luxury-DMC villa AOR","mor_posture":true,"note":"no branded ultra hotel in-village; top villa tier","source":"https://www.rentalescapes.com/rentals/luxury-vacation-rentals-mexico/riviera-maya/akumal"},{"name":"Rosewood Mayakoba (~35-40 min north)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"note":"nearest true ultra hotel","source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"Banyan Tree / Andaz-Alila Mayakoba","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"},{"name":"La Casa de la Playa (Grupo Xcaret)","price_tier":"ultra","virtuoso":true,"earning":"15% via Xcaret Agents Pro OR host-Virtuoso ($100 credit)","mor_posture":true,"source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/hotels/16561922/la-casa-de-la-playa"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Akumal, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.3958,"lng":-87.3153}}'::jsonb, 3),
  ('ambergris-caye-belize', '10S', 'Ambergris Caye / San Pedro', 'Belize', 'Ambergris Caye Belize', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Belize', '{"tropical","liveaboard","romance","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Belize''s largest island and #1 tourism engine; runs parallel to the UNESCO Belize Barrier Reef, ~35 mi NE of Belize City.","Hol Chan Marine Reserve (est. 1987, ~4 mi south of San Pedro) protects ~18 km2 with 160+ fish species; Shark Ray Alley added 1999.","Belize''s national recompression capability is on-island: SSS hyperbaric chamber (since 1989) + DAN-affiliated Belize Chamber Project (2015), both 24/7.","Air access via BZE Philip Goldson Intl -> SPR San Pedro, ~20-min puddle-jumper (Tropic Air / Maya Island Air) or ~90-min water taxi via Caye Caulker.","English is Belize''s official language - the only English-official nation in Central America."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (also 90); San Pedro Police 206-2022; San Pedro Coast Guard 222-5260","hyperbaric_chamber":"YES - on Ambergris/San Pedro: SSS Belize Hyperbaric Facility (est. 1989, 4-diver lock, US Navy tables, 24/7) + DAN-affiliated Belize Chamber Project (2015). National dive-safety asset.","hospital":"Lighthouse Medical Center (San Pedro, private) for urgent care; serious trauma -> Karl Heusner Memorial Hospital (KHMH), Belize City - the only trauma centre in Belize; then US evac. Island remoteness flagged.","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"cayes/San Pedro open; only Southside Belize City (Haulover Creek Canal to Fabers Road) restricted","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"malaria":"none on the cayes; Belize WHO-certified malaria-free 2023; small mainland Cayo District cluster (Apr 2025) - mainland only","water":"do not drink tap water on the cayes; use bottled/filtered","mosquito_borne":"dengue primary concern; also chikungunya, Zika (day-biting Aedes) - use repellent","founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on the BOOK WITH WARNING bin (Four-Bin v3): full verbatim live US State Dept advisory disclosed + acknowledged at booking; only Southside Belize City is the named danger"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-12-20","peak":"late-Dec through April (dry season); dive peak extends to June","fire_date":"2026-12-08","fire_date_secondary":"2026-11-01 (Mar-Apr dive/whale-shark surge, 4-6 mo lead)","shoulder":"September-November (wet/green season, lower rates)","green":"September-November","booking_lead":"4-6 months (dive/liveaboard/atoll + ultra private-island)","off_season_specials":"green-season weekly/monthly villa & condo discounts","event_peaks":["San Pedro Lobster Festival (early summer; 2026 advertised Jul 1-12)","Costa Maya Festival (August; 2026 dates unverified)"],"whale_shark_window":"Mar-Jun full-moon (2026 full moons Mar 14, Apr 13); Apr-May best"},"jewels":[{"name":"Hol Chan Marine Reserve (Zone A)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","status":"live","hook":"Signature 30-ft dive/snorkel; moray, turtles, 160+ fish species in a protected channel.","bookable_category":"guided dive/snorkel","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"David CLIA dive lane","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hol_Chan_Marine_Reserve + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","blurb":"Signature 30-ft dive/snorkel; moray, turtles, 160+ fish species in a protected channel.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"David CLIA dive lane","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Shark Ray Alley (Zone D)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","status":"live","hook":"Guided shallow encounter with docile nurse sharks and southern stingrays.","bookable_category":"guided snorkel/dive","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"David CLIA dive lane","source":"https://ambergrisdivers.com/trip/snorkeling-hol-chan-shark-ray-alley-marine-reserve/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","blurb":"Guided shallow encounter with docile nurse sharks and southern stingrays.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"David CLIA dive lane","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Mexico Rocks & Tres Cocos","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","status":"live","hook":"Shallow patch-reef gardens north of town; ideal for new divers and long snorkels.","bookable_category":"guided dive/snorkel","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"David CLIA dive lane","source":"https://www.backpackerswanderlust.com/diving-in-ambergris-caye-belize/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","blurb":"Shallow patch-reef gardens north of town; ideal for new divers and long snorkels.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"David CLIA dive lane","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Great Blue Hole + Lighthouse Reef","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","status":"live","hook":"Bucket-list 410-ft UNESCO sinkhole; full-day boat or scenic-flight-and-dive combo.","bookable_category":"dive expedition / air combo","tier":"premier","commission_path":"David CLIA dive lane + air affiliate","source":"https://ambergrisdivers.com/trip/great-blue-hole-dive-and-lighthouse-reef-day-tour/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","blurb":"Bucket-list 410-ft UNESCO sinkhole; full-day boat or scenic-flight-and-dive combo.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"David CLIA dive lane + air affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Bacalar Chico National Park & Marine Reserve","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","status":"live","hook":"Remote far-north reef, mangrove and Maya-history diving near the Mexico border.","bookable_category":"dive expedition / private charter","tier":"premier","commission_path":"David CLIA dive lane","source":"https://www.viaventure.com/destinations/belize/ambergris-caye/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","blurb":"Remote far-north reef, mangrove and Maya-history diving near the Mexico border.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"David CLIA dive lane","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Grand Slam fly-fishing (bonefish + permit + tarpon)","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"400+ sq mi of flats; El Pescador Orvis-endorsed base; all three species in a day.","bookable_category":"lodge / guided angling","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"CLIA + Fora (lodge/villa)","source":"https://www.elpescador.com/articles/from-bonefish-to-tarpon-the-anglers-guide-to-el-pescadors-grand-slam/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"400+ sq mi of flats; El Pescador Orvis-endorsed base; all three species in a day.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"CLIA + Fora (lodge/villa)","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Gladden Spit whale-shark encounter","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Mar-Jun full-moon aggregation; snorkel/dive with whale sharks (mainland-launched marquee day-add).","bookable_category":"guided dive/snorkel","tier":"premier","commission_path":"David CLIA dive lane","source":"https://belizescuba.com/diving-snorkeling/whale-sharks/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","si":"GEA","blurb":"Mar-Jun full-moon aggregation; snorkel/dive with whale sharks (mainland-launched marquee day-add).","commission":"David CLIA dive lane","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Caye Caulker day trip","si_tag":"GEA","status":"live","hook":"Car-free ''go slow'' sister island 30 min by boat; the Split, cheaper eats.","bookable_category":"day tour / water taxi","tier":"essential","commission_path":"tour affiliate (Viator) + water taxi","source":"https://www.viaventure.com/destinations/belize/ambergris-caye/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"GEA","blurb":"Car-free ''go slow'' sister island 30 min by boat; the Split, cheaper eats.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"tour affiliate (Viator) + water taxi","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Secret Beach (west side)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Famous shallow-lagoon bar-and-beach scene; golf-cart destination, calm swim water.","bookable_category":"day trip / F&B","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"tour + F&B affiliate","source":"https://agentsgather.com/vacation-rentals-ambergris-caye-belize/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","blurb":"Famous shallow-lagoon bar-and-beach scene; golf-cart destination, calm swim water.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"tour + F&B affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"San Pedro town + Belikin nightlife","si_tag":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","status":"live","hook":"Sand-street town core, dockside bars, live music, Lobster Festival hub.","bookable_category":"F&B / event","tier":"essential","commission_path":"F&B / event affiliate","source":"https://www.thephoenixbelize.com/explore-more/ultimate-guide-belize-lobster-season-san-pedro + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands / Beaches","blurb":"Sand-street town core, dockside bars, live music, Lobster Festival hub.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"F&B / event affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"},{"name":"Sunset sail / private charter","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Champagne catamaran sail over the reef lagoon; the honeymoon signature.","bookable_category":"charter / activity","tier":"premier","commission_path":"Fora / activity affiliate","source":"https://www.viaventure.com/destinations/belize/ambergris-caye/ + Accessed 2026-07-06","timing":"late-Dec through April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Champagne catamaran sail over the reef lagoon; the honeymoon signature.","when":"late-Dec through April","commission":"Fora / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-06"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the best diving and snorkeling on Ambergris Caye?","a":"Start at Hol Chan Marine Reserve and Shark Ray Alley. The signature ~30-ft channel dive delivers moray, turtles and 160+ fish species, while Shark Ray Alley — added as Zone D in 1999 — puts you in shallow water with docile 4–6 ft nurse sharks and southern stingrays. Both are guided, beginner-friendly profiles because they are shallow and protected.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Do you need a car on Ambergris Caye?","a":"No — the island runs on golf carts, not cars, and beachfront San Pedro properties sit a 10-minute walk from the airstrip and steps from the water-taxi dock. English is the official language (Belize is the only English-official nation in Central America), so North American travelers move through town with zero language friction.","source":"agentsgather.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Where should you stay for a honeymoon on Ambergris Caye?","a":"For seclusion, Cayo Espanto is a private island 3 miles off San Pedro with 7 all-inclusive villas and an 18-guest cap from ~US$1,695/villa/night; for adults-only boutique romance, Matachica offers thatched casitas. Both read romance-forward because the property caps guest count and builds the stay around couples.","source":"aprivateisland.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you fish the Grand Slam from Ambergris Caye?","a":"Yes — Ambergris fronts 400+ sq mi of flats, channels and lagoons where bonefish, permit and tarpon can all be landed in one day, with El Pescador the Orvis-endorsed base for 50+ years. Tarpon peaks July–September; bonefish and permit run year-round, so the slam is a realistic single-day target.","source":"elpescador.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Ambergris Caye safe right now?","a":"Yes, with the standard disclosure. Belize is at US State Dept Level 3 (reissued June 18, 2026, code C/Crime only), but the only geographically named restricted area is Southside Belize City — the cayes and San Pedro are explicitly open and tourist-friendly. Fly or water-taxi in via the tourist corridor and you never touch the named zone.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-06-18","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on Ambergris Caye?","a":"Island remoteness for serious medical events, not crime. San Pedro''s Lighthouse Medical Center handles urgent care, but serious trauma routes to Karl Heusner Memorial Hospital in Belize City — the only trauma centre in Belize — then to the US, requiring air/water transfer off the island. Dengue is the primary mosquito-borne concern; there is no malaria on the cayes (Belize was WHO-certified malaria-free in 2023).","source":"belizetravelinsider.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving the Great Blue Hole dangerous?","a":"It is an advanced dive, not a beginner novelty. The Blue Hole bottoms below recreational limits (~410 ft total); recreational dives target ~130 ft along the stalactite ledges, so treat it as advanced/technical-adjacent with sound gas planning. The offshore boat crossing is 2.5–3 hours each way, or ~20 minutes by scenic flight from San Pedro.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ambergris Caye & San Pedro, Belize: Dive the Reef, Stay Well | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Belize''s #1 island — dive Hol Chan and Shark Ray Alley, honeymoon at Cayo Espanto or Matachica, chase the Grand Slam on the flats. National hyperbaric chamber on-island. TravelWell.","slug":"ambergris-caye-belize","primary_keyword":"Ambergris Caye Belize","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Ambergris Caye Belize","San Pedro Belize diving","Hol Chan Marine Reserve snorkel","Ambergris Caye honeymoon resort","Cayo Espanto private island Belize","Belize barrier reef diving","Ambergris Caye villa rental","Shark Ray Alley tour","Belize Grand Slam fly fishing","Great Blue Hole day trip San Pedro"],"hreflang":["en"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"Dive Liveaboards / Reef Diving","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Cayo Espanto","why_ultra":"Private-island, 7 all-inclusive seafront villas incl. overwater Casa Ventanas, 18-guest cap, 24-hr dedicated houseman, chef-tailored meals, whole-island buyout.","earning":"Fora lane (AOR commissionable)","virtuoso_value_add":"resort credit / arrival amenity / upgrade on availability where consortia-eligible (confirm preferred status)","mor":"commissionable AOR (not merchant)","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Victoria House Resort & Spa","why_ultra":"Five-star colonial-Caribbean flagship, spa, personalized service; ranks with the island''s top hotels.","earning":"Fora lane (AOR commissionable)","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenity where eligible","mor":"commissionable AOR","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Matachica Resort & Spa","why_ultra":"Adults-only boutique, private thatched casitas, romance-forward.","earning":"Fora lane (AOR commissionable)","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenity where eligible","mor":"commissionable AOR","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Las Terrazas","why_ultra":"Design-led north-shore residences, full kitchens, sea-view balconies.","earning":"Fora lane (AOR commissionable)","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenity where eligible","mor":"commissionable AOR","tier":"luxury"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Ambergris Caye / San Pedro, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.9214,"lng":-87.9611}}'::jsonb, 4)
