  ('bacalar-mexico', '10S', 'Bacalar', 'Mexico', '*If it''s the water so still and so many', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"tropical","wellness","adventure"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Lagoon of Seven Colors - karst-fed (no river inputs), colors from depth/sand/cenotes/light","Active living-stromatolite colony (cyanobacteria, ~3.5B-yr lineage); <12 such colonies worldwide","Cenote Azul - one of Mexico''s largest open-air cenotes, ~70m across x up to ~90m deep","Eco-luxury cluster: Habitas Bacalar + Boca de Agua (future Wellness SI anchor)","Freshwater destination (no dive-cert node); ~3.5-4h south of Cancun - a stay-2-nights slow trip"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","nearest_trauma":"Chetumal (Hospital General, ~40 min south) or evac to Cancun","malaria":"NONE in tourist zone; dengue present","water":"bottled/purified","hurricane":"Jun-Nov, peak Aug-Oct","special_rule":"STROMATOLITE PROTECTION - no touch, no regular sunscreen (biodegradable only/none); a single handprint damages years of growth"},"timing":{"peak":"Dry season Nov-Apr (calm-water AM); Dec-Apr hardest to book, Jan/Mar busiest","shoulder":"Nov and Feb-Mar (best value in dry window; avoid Semana Santa)","green":"Rainy Jun-Sep (afternoon showers, hurricane overlap) - fill-the-beds","booking_window_lead_time":"Longer than regional avg for dock-front/lagoon-front; best waterfront stock clears first for Dec-Apr","fill_the_beds":"Jun-Sep green + Nov/early-Dec shoulder; sell slow-travel/wellness (yoga, dawn paddle)","holiday_event_peaks":"Semana Santa (domestic crush), Dec holiday + New Year","campaign_start_trigger":"Live ~4-6 months ahead of Nov-Apr (by ~Jun-Jul); secondary green-season value push for Jun-Sep","source":"https://hellobacalar.com/guides/best-time-visit-bacalar"},"jewels":[{"name":"Los Rapidos + Canal de los Piratas sailboat circuit","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"lagoon tour","commission_path":"affiliate ~4-8% (Viator/GYG) or lodge direct","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/bacalar-lagoon/","hook":"half-day sail across the color bands past the pirate channel ·","si":"tropical","blurb":"half-day sail across the color bands past the pirate channel ·","commission":"affiliate ~4-8% (Viator/GYG) or lodge direct"},{"name":"Cenote Azul open-air swim","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable_category":"cenote entry","commission_path":"non-commissionable gate; bundle into day-tour","source":"https://kendyltravels.com/bacalar-cenotes/","hook":"~70 m-wide, ~90 m-deep sky cenote with rim restaurant ·","si":"tropical","blurb":"~70 m-wide, ~90 m-deep sky cenote with rim restaurant ·","commission":"non-commissionable gate; bundle into day-tour"},{"name":"Cenote Negro (seventh color)","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"lagoon tour","commission_path":"affiliate via tour","source":"https://kendyltravels.com/bacalar-cenotes/","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the deep-blue cenote said to complete the seven colors ·","si":"tropical","blurb":"the deep-blue cenote said to complete the seven colors ·","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate via tour"},{"name":"Stromatolite kayak (Cenote Cocalitos)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"guided eco-tour","commission_path":"guided-tour affiliate; no-touch/no-sunscreen mandatory","source":"https://sandinmycurls.com/bacalar-mexico-seven-color-lagoon-guide/","si":"adventure","commission":"guided-tour affiliate; no-touch/no-sunscreen mandatory"},{"name":"Eco-luxury lagoon lodge (Habitas / Boca de Agua)","si_tag":"wellness","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable_category":"boutique lodging","commission_path":"on application, 10%+ boutique/luxury","source":"https://www.bocadeagua.com/blog/best-hotels-bacalar-mexico","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"thatched cabins, yoga, clear kayaks, lagoon-front restaurant ·","si":"wellness","blurb":"thatched cabins, yoga, clear kayaks, lagoon-front restaurant ·","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"on application, 10%+ boutique/luxury"},{"name":"Sunrise kayak + slow-water day","si_tag":"wellness","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"lodge activity","commission_path":"bundled in lodge rate","source":"https://www.bocadeagua.com/","si":"wellness","commission":"bundled in lodge rate"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Bacalar safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes - freely bookable, no hold. Bacalar sits in Quintana Roo (US State Dept Level 2, Exercise Increased Caution, dated 2026-05-29). It''s a quiet lagoon town; the nearest full trauma hospital is Chetumal (~40 min south), with higher-acuity cases evacuated to Cancun.","source":"travel.state.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bacalar?","a":"Open-water swimming discipline, mosquitoes and hurricanes - not crime. Cenote Azul is a sky-facing sinkhole up to ~90m deep with no floor, so treat it as open water (strong swimmers/life vests); use repellent for dengue (present, worse in the rainy season); hurricane season runs Jun-Nov, peaking Aug-Oct.","source":"kendyltravels.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is it safe - and allowed - to swim near the stromatolites?","a":"Yes to swimming the lagoon, but the stromatolites are strictly no-touch and no-sunscreen. Do not touch, stand on, or apply regular sunscreen near the colonies - a single handprint can destroy years of microbial growth - so view and photograph from a kayak only, using biodegradable sunscreen or none. Bacalar is not a scuba destination, so there are no dive or no-fly considerations.","source":"sandinmycurls.com","si_tag":"globaladv"},{"q":"What is the Lagoon of Seven Colors, and how do you see it?","a":"It''s a karst-fed freshwater lagoon whose colors shift from turquoise to navy over its sand, cenotes and varying depths. The signature way to see it is a half-day catamaran or sailboat circuit past Los Rapidos, the stromatolites and the Canal de los Piratas; go on a calm morning when the water is glass-still.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Which are the best eco-luxury places to stay in Bacalar?","a":"Boca de Agua and Our Habitas Bacalar lead the lagoon. Boca de Agua is a Frida Escobedo-designed set of ~26 stilted treehouse villas on 82 acres with a MICHELIN Key 2025; Our Habitas is the established adults-only, wellness-led lagoon retreat ~20 min south of town. Both are direct/consortia bookings - book waterfront stock early for Dec-Apr.","source":"mrandmrssmith.com","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Bacalar?","a":"November-April, the dry season, is best - warm, mostly dry, with glass-still calm-water mornings. Within that, November and Feb-March are the best value (avoid Semana Santa); the rainy green season, Jun-Sep, is lush, quiet and cheapest but brings afternoon showers and hurricane overlap.","source":"hellobacalar.com","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bacalar Mexico: Lagoon of Seven Colors & Stromatolites","meta_description":"Bacalar''s Lagoon of Seven Colors, living stromatolites and open-air cenotes - where to sail, swim and stay, and how to protect what you came to see.","slug":"bacalar-mexico","primary_keyword":"Bacalar Lagoon of Seven Colors","long_tail":["Bacalar stromatolites","Cenote Azul Bacalar","Bacalar eco lodges","Bacalar sailboat tour","Bacalar things to do"],"search_language":"bilingual (en + es-MX)","local_keywords":["Laguna de los Siete Colores","Bacalar que hacer","estromatolitos Bacalar","Cenote Azul Bacalar","hoteles Bacalar laguna","tour velero Bacalar","mejor epoca para visitar Bacalar"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister - commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Quintana Roo US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution, dated 2026-05-29) - freely bookable; the real planning is open-water swim discipline + stromatolite protection + hurricane season, not crime; MXN currency"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":5,"misses":17,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; FRESHWATER lagoon - Dive Globally is a MISS (no scuba/cenote-cert node here, unlike Cozumel/Chinchorro); sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"wellness","name":"wellness","status":"future"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Boca de Agua","price_tier":"ultra","what":"Frida Escobedo-designed eco-luxury, ~26 stilted treehouse villas on 82 acres, MICHELIN Key 2025","bookable":"direct + Mr & Mrs Smith (Hyatt) + MICHELIN Guide Hotels","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso-or-Smith consortia","mor_posture":"broker to property/consortia; property-paid commission; no net-rate resale","direct_only_flag":false,"source":"https://www.mrandmrssmith.com/luxury-hotels/boca-de-agua"},{"name":"Our Habitas Bacalar","price_tier":"luxury-ultra","what":"Most established luxe-eco resort; adults-only, lagoon A-frame tents + jungle rooms, holistic wellness/spa","bookable":"direct + Mr & Mrs Smith + Ownia Collection","earning":"on application / host-consortia","mor_posture":"broker to property/consortia; property-paid commission","direct_only_flag":false,"source":"https://www.ourhabitas.com/bacalar/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Bacalar, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":18.6767,"lng":-88.3953}}'::jsonb, 7),
  ('balandra-beach-mexico', '10S', 'Balandra Beach (Playa Balandra)', 'Mexico', 'Balandra beach La Paz', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Baja California Sur (Los Cabos & La Paz)', '{"tropical","family","romance"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["CONANP Natural Protected Area since 2008; ~25 km north of La Paz","Two fixed daily shifts (08:00-12:00 / 13:00-17:00), ~450 visitors per slot, first-come","Conservation bracelet required ~MXN 125 pp/day (under-12s, seniors/retirees, disabilities exempt with ID)","No commercial food service inside the bay; limited services (toilets/info) - bring own water/shade/snacks","El Hongo mushroom rock is the emblem of Balandra and La Paz; shallow calm turquoise water"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"limited on-site (toilets/info only); serious cases ~25 km to La Paz - Hospital Salvatierra/ISSSTE/private + air-evac; carry medical insurance","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"effectively none in Baja California Sur","dengue":"circulates in Mexico - use repellent","water":"carry own bottled/purified water - no services in the bay","hurricane":"Jun-Nov - trip insurance for summer/fall","day_use":"TIMED-ENTRY two shifts + ~450/slot cap, first-come, arrive >=30 min early; CONANP bracelet required; NO food vendors inside","sun_heat":"scarce shade - umbrella, hat, reef-safe sunscreen, ample water","el_hongo":"protected/restored rock - do not climb or touch","swimming":"shallow, calm, family-safe but NO lifeguards - supervise children, watch outgoing tide; no diving (wading/kayak beach)"},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry desert winter, comfortable) - slot cap fills fastest, arrive early; rides La Paz high season","shoulder":"May & Sep-Oct (warm, quieter slots, easier entry)","green":"Jun-Aug (summer heat + hurricane window, scarce shade - early-slot only; domestic holidays spike)","booking_window_lead_time":"no lodging to pre-book; conservation bracelet is same-day/short-lead (CONANP digital or La Paz office); binding constraint is daily slot cap (~450/shift) - plan day, arrive early; book La Paz lodging on 3-6-month peak lead","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"morning Balandra slot + Playa Tecolote (vendors allowed) + Malecon afternoon; sell as half-day postcard-beach anchor of a La Paz stay year-round","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa (Easter), Mexican summer holidays - domestic surges hit slot cap hardest","campaign_start_trigger":"add-on jewel, not standalone - market inside La Paz/Baja campaigns (Nov-Apr beach campaigns late summer; summer value in spring), always paired with La Paz lodging + transfer","flag":"no wildlife season; peak = weather + La Paz volume + Mexican holidays; NO lodging on-beach; hard visitor cap","sources":["https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","https://beachythings.site/playa-balandra-entrance-fee-rules/","https://mrplayas.com/la-paz/beaches"]},"jewels":[{"name":"El Hongo mushroom-rock walk + swim","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"beach-day tour/transfer + CONANP bracelet or self-drive","commission_path":"DMC transfer + Viator/GYG affiliate","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puerto_Balandra,_Baja_California_Sur","hook":"wade the shallow flats to Baja''s most-photographed rock, the emblem of La Paz","si":"tropical","blurb":"wade the shallow flats to Baja''s most-photographed rock, the emblem of La Paz","commission":"DMC transfer + Viator/GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Kayak / SUP the turquoise flats","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable":"local kayak/SUP rental/tour","commission_path":"operator + GYG affiliate","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","hook":"paddle glass-calm, waist-deep water around the coves; low-impact, all-ages","si":"tropical","blurb":"paddle glass-calm, waist-deep water around the coves; low-impact, all-ages","commission":"operator + GYG affiliate"},{"name":"Shallow-water kids'' beach day","si_tag":"family","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"beach-day transfer + bracelet","commission_path":"DMC transfer + affiliate","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","hook":"near-waveless, waist-deep flats — one of Baja''s safest child-friendly swims","si":"family","blurb":"near-waveless, waist-deep flats — one of Baja''s safest child-friendly swims","commission":"DMC transfer + affiliate"},{"name":"Balandra + Tecolote combo day","si_tag":"family","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable":"combined beach-day tour","commission_path":"local operator + Viator affiliate","source":"https://mrplayas.com/la-paz/beaches","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"pair protected Balandra with nearby Playa Tecolote for a full family beach day","si":"family","blurb":"pair protected Balandra with nearby Playa Tecolote for a full family beach day","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"local operator + Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Sunrise/early-slot photo morning","si_tag":"romance","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"private driver-guide + bracelet","commission_path":"Journey Mexico/Amstar DMC + affiliate","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"postcard turquoise + El Hongo before the crowds and heat — couples'' shoot backdrop","si":"romance","blurb":"postcard turquoise + El Hongo before the crowds and heat — couples'' shoot backdrop","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Journey Mexico/Amstar DMC + affiliate"}],"faq":[{"q":"How do I get into Balandra, and what does it cost?","a":"Arrive at least 30 minutes before your shift and buy a conservation bracelet — Balandra is not a walk-up-anytime beach. Entry runs in two fixed daily slots (08:00–12:00, 13:00–17:00), capped near 450 visitors each on a first-come basis, with a ~MXN 125 pp/day CONANP bracelet (exemptions for under-12s, seniors and people with disabilities).","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Balandra safe for young children?","a":"Yes — it is one of Baja''s gentlest swims, because the bay is near-waveless and only waist-deep across much of its width. But there are no lifeguards and no vendors inside, so supervise kids closely, watch the outgoing tide over the flats, and pack your own water, shade and food.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"When is the best time for photos at El Hongo?","a":"Take the 08:00 morning slot in the cooler Nov–Apr months for the best light and the emptiest sand. Balandra fills its ~450-per-slot cap fastest in peak season and over Mexican holidays, and midday desert glare flattens the turquoise — so the early shift gives couples both the calm water and the postcard color.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is Balandra safe to visit right now?","a":"Yes — freely bookable. Baja California Sur carries a US State Dept Level 2 \"Exercise Increased Caution\" (maintained May 29, 2026), the standard tier for Mexico''s resort states, and BCS is among the country''s safer states.","source":"travel.state.gov","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Balandra?","a":"Sun, heat and the lack of services — not crime. There is scarce shade, no food or water vendors and no lifeguards inside the bay, and hurricane season runs Jun–Nov; bring an umbrella, hydration and reef-safe sunscreen, and carry trip insurance for summer/fall dates.","source":"dossier","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Balandra Beach La Paz: El Hongo & Entry Rules 2026","meta_description":"Wade the shallow turquoise flats of protected Playa Balandra to El Hongo mushroom rock — timed entry (~450/slot), conservation bracelet, no services. Plan the day.","slug":"balandra-beach-mexico","primary_keyword":"Balandra beach La Paz","long_tail":["Balandra beach entrance fee 2026","Playa Balandra timed entry rules","El Hongo mushroom rock La Paz","Balandra vs Tecolote beach","Balandra shallow water family beach"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Playa Balandra La Paz horarios","brazalete Balandra CONANP precio","El Hongo de Balandra","playa protegida La Paz aguas someras","Balandra vs Tecolote","Playa Balandra niños familia","cómo llegar a Balandra La Paz"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Quintana Roo/Mexico US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution) - freely bookable; MXN currency, USD widely accepted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":3,"misses":19,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW"},{"si":"family","name":"family","status":"future","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW"},{"si":"romance","name":"Romance, Marriages & Honeymoons","status":"future","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private driver-guide Balandra morning (from La Paz/Los Cabos luxury base)","posture":"no on-beach lodging exists; ultra play is private guide + early-slot + provisioning","price_tier":"luxury","earning":"on application via host / Journey Mexico DMC","virtuoso_value_add":"private guide + chilled provisioning (no vendors) + pairing with Espiritu Santo","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/balandra-beach-mexico/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Balandra Beach (Playa Balandra), Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":24.32,"lng":-110.33}}'::jsonb, 8),
  ('banos-ecuador', '10S', 'Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador', 'Ecuador', 'Baños de Agua Santa', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Andes (Quito) & Galápagos', '{"wellness","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_note":"Mainland L4 (Do Not Travel): Esmeraldas city/north, Guayaquil south of Portete de Tarqui Ave, Durán canton, Huaquillas/Arenillas. Baños/Tungurahua province not named in any L3/L4 zone.","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":"No airport in Baños — access via UIO (Mariscal Sucre, Quito) + ~3-3.5 hr road transfer (~180 km)","altitude_m":1820,"altitude_notes":{"banos_m":1820,"casa_del_arbol_runtun_m":2600,"mild_ams":"uncommon at town level (1,820m); watch if arriving from Quito 2,850m or higher paramo; exertion at 2,600m viewpoints is real work","trauma":"Local hospital for stabilization; serious trauma routes to Ambato (~40 min) then Quito (~3-3.5 hr); complex cases evac to US (Miami)"},"volcano":{"name":"Tungurahua","type":"active stratovolcano (~5,023m)","status_2026":"background / very-low IG-EPN alert; no eruption activity; 24/7 monitoring; UNESCO Geopark (2025)","history":"near-continuous eruption 1999-2016, quiet since 2016","rule":"Re-verify live IG-EPN status before each booking; know town ashfall/lahar evacuation routes","monitoring_source":"https://www.igepn.edu.ec/tungurahua"},"water":"not reliably potable — bottled/filtered (distinct from thermal-bath waters, for soaking not drinking)","advisory_source":"https://travel.state.gov/en/international-travel/travel-advisories/ecuador.html (Level 2)"},"timing":{"peak":["Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec","Jan","Feb"],"shoulder_green":["Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug"],"inflection":["Aug","Feb","Mar"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-Aug for the Sep-Feb dry peak; 1-2 weeks ahead of Ecuadorian holiday weekends/Carnaval/Semana Santa); fire 