/ chiva)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Bike-hire + guided-route/chiva-tour affiliate (fall/cable fees non-comm.)","source":"https://southamericabackpacker.com/ruta-de-las-cascadas-banos/","hook":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","si":"expedition","blurb":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","commission":"Bike-hire + guided-route/chiva-tour affiliate (fall/cable fees non-comm.)"},{"name":"Canyoning — Río Blanco","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Local adventure-operator booking (Geotours/Ivagatours) — guided-only","source":"https://www.geotoursbanios.com/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local adventure-operator booking (Geotours/Ivagatours) — guided-only"},{"name":"Whitewater rafting — Río Pastaza (Class III-IV)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Local operator + activity affiliate","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-tours/White-Water-Rafting/d22150-g17-c27534","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local operator + activity affiliate"},{"name":"Mirador Bellavista","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Guided town-and-viewpoint walk affiliate or self-guided add-on","source":"https://www.ecuatouring.com/banos-travel-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","si":"expedition","blurb":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","when":"year-round","commission":"Guided town-and-viewpoint walk affiliate or self-guided add-on"},{"name":"Termas de la Virgen thermal baths (at night)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Entry non-commissionable — monetize spa-hotel room-night + private spa add-on","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g312857-d20120113-Reviews-Termas_de_la_Virgen-Banos_Tungurahua_Province.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","si":"romance","blurb":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","when":"year-round","commission":"Entry non-commissionable — monetize spa-hotel room-night + private spa add-on"},{"name":"Luna Volcán / former Luna Runtún — spa with volcano view","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank; property/wing buyout for weddings","source":"https://www.booking.com/hotel/ec/luna-volcan-adventure-spa.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","si":"romance","blurb":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank; property/wing buyout for weddings"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort (converted monastery)","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank — future Wellness SI anchor","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/ecuador/samari.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank — future Wellness SI anchor"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the \"Swing at the End of the World\" worth it — and how much?","a":"Yes, and it is cheap — it is the image that put Baños on a million screens. The Casa del Árbol treehouse swing launches you out over the Tungurahua gorge from the Runtún ridge at ~2,600 m; the complex opens 07:00–19:00, entry is ~$1, and staff clip you into a climbing harness on a steel-beam frame.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where can couples soak in thermal baths at night in Baños?","a":"At the Termas de la Virgen, in the town center beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall. Its sulfate-rich pools are heated by Tungurahua, open 05:00–17:00 and again 18:00–22:00, at ~$4 adult entry — the signature romantic-and-restorative Baños ritual, best paired with a volcano-view spa-hotel room-night.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is Baños a genuine wellness and spa destination?","a":"Increasingly, yes — the town''s name literally means \"Baths of Holy Water.\" The anchor is Samari Spa Resort, a 300-year-old former Jesuit monastery on ~10 acres with a heated indoor pool, sauna, Turkish bath, whirlpool and full spa, ranked among Baños''s top hotels — mineral-rich thermal springs fed by Tungurahua''s volcanic heat make Baños a natural wellness base.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wellness-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Baños Ecuador safe right now?","a":"Yes — Baños is freely bookable with no consent flow. Ecuador is at State Department Level 2 (Exercise Increased Caution), but Baños/Tungurahua province is explicitly not named in any Level 3 or Level 4 zone — the country''s L4 \"Do Not Travel\" corridors are all coastal (Esmeraldas, Guayaquil-south, Durán, Huaquillas/Arenillas). `book_enabled = true`.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Baños?","a":"Not urban crime — the load-bearing risk is activity risk. ~88% of Ecuador''s homicides occur in five coastal provinces, and the Andean highlands including Baños run below the homicide rates of many mid-sized US cities; the town''s core product is adrenaline (canyoning, Class III–IV rafting, the swing, highway cycling), so guided-vs-unguided is the whole game.","source":"myecuadorvisa.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Tungurahua volcano dangerous right now?","a":"It is a real, live geohazard held quiet by monitoring — not a decorative caveat. Tungurahua erupted near-continuously 1999–2016, then went quiet; as of mid-2026 IG-EPN reports background/very-low activity with no precursor signals and 24/7 instrument monitoring, so any escalation would trigger alerts well in advance. Re-verify live IG-EPN status before booking.","source":"igepn.edu.ec, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is canyoning or the swing in Baños dangerous?","a":"Both carry real, activity-specific risk that guiding and gear mitigate. Canyoning on the Río Blanco is a guided-only roped waterfall-descent sport (helmet, harness, wetsuit, certified guide); the Casa del Árbol swing is 18+ with a ~220 lb (100 kg) weight limit and requires the operator''s climbing harness every ride. Never freelance either — book reputable operators like Geotours or Ivagatours.","source":"geotoursbanios.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador — The Swing, Waterfalls, Rafting & Thermal Baths | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Baños Ecuador","Casa del Árbol columpio","columpio fin del mundo Baños","Pailón del Diablo","Ruta de las Cascadas","rafting río Pastaza Baños","canyoning Baños","Termas de la Virgen","volcán Tungurahua estado","hoteles con spa en Baños"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Baños de Agua Santa"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Luna Volcán, Adventure SPA (formerly Luna Runtún)","category":"Boutique adventure-spa on Tungurahua''s flank, 30 rooms, 35-ha forest","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; Fora/host-agency on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort","category":"300-yr converted-monastery spa resort, ~10 acres","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; host-agency/Fora on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Casa del Suizo","category":"Amazon-edge Napo River jungle lodge (Ahuano), 75 rooms","mor":"DMC package / luxury-specialist — the Amazon-extend upsell","tier":"$$$-$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-1.3928,"lng":-78.4269}}'::jsonb, 9),
  ('blue-hole-belize', '10S', 'The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole', 'Belize', 'Atolls, walls and the Blue Hole **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Belize', '{"liveaboard","expedition","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Great Blue Hole is 318 m (1,043 ft) across and 124 m (407 ft) deep, near the center of Lighthouse Reef ~70 km (43 mi) off Belize City.","Belize has three coral atolls — Turneffe, Lighthouse Reef, Glover''s Reef — within the UNESCO-listed Belize Barrier Reef Reserve System.","Blue Hole stalactites hang at ~100-140 ft (30-42 m); the dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft with a narrow no-deco window — Advanced cert recommended.","Belize Aggressor III/IV depart Belize City Saturdays, up to 5 dives/day, 24-27 dives on a 7-night charter (39-42 on 10-night).","Whale sharks gather at Gladden Spit (southern Belize) around the full moon March-June."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Belize Chamber Project Ltd, San Pedro (Ambergris Caye) — only DAN-Preferred chamber in Belize, 24/7; hours of boat+air transit from the offshore atolls","advisory_date":"2026-06-18","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) only","book_enabled":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; offshore atolls open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco dive / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before BZE flight home","water":"open Caribbean ocean; no malaria offshore; high sun/sea exposure; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory"},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar","dive_calendar":true,"curve_start":"2026-02-15","peak":"March-June (Blue Hole best flat seas April-June)","whale_shark_window":["2026-03-14","2026-04-13","2026-05-12","2026-06-11"],"booking_lead_months":"4-6 (peak charters / full-boat buyouts longer)","shoulder_green_season":"September-November (wet/rougher, off-season fill)","fire_date":"2026-02-01","trigger_date":"2026-02-01","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor charter availability + whale-shark sighting logs; flat-sea onset shifts yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Great Blue Hole (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Aggressor)","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Blue_Hole","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","blurb":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Aggressor)"},{"name":"Half Moon Caye Wall + Natural Monument","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane; park fee non-commissionable","source":"https://ambergriscaye.com/pages/town/divelighthouse.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","si":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","blurb":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","when":"year-round","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane; park fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"The Painted Wall & Quebrada (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"liveaboard","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/Belize","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane"},{"name":"Turneffe Elbow (Turneffe Atoll)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or Fora via Turneffe resorts","source":"https://www.divessi.com/en/mydiveguide/divesite/98293","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or Fora via Turneffe resorts"},{"name":"Glover''s Reef (remote atoll)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","commission_path":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane (scarcity — few boats reach it)","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane (scarcity — few boats reach it)"},{"name":"Gladden Spit whale sharks (seasonal, southern Belize)","si_tag":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"AFF/day-operator or Fora via Placencia; marine-reserve fee non-commissionable","source":"https://belizescuba.com/diving-snorkeling/whale-sharks/","si":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","commission":"AFF/day-operator or Fora via Placencia; marine-reserve fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Tobacco Caye","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Fora lane (small guesthouse packages)","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora lane (small guesthouse packages)"},{"name":"Long Caye (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on operator","source":"https://www.belizehighcommission.com/areas-of-belize/lighthouse-reef-bz","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on operator"}],"faq":[{"q":"How many dives do you get on a Belize Aggressor liveaboard trip?","a":"Up to five dives a day — 24–27 dives on a 7-night charter, 39–42 on a 10-night. The Aggressor III/IV depart the Fort George dock in Belize City every Saturday at 6 pm, dive Sunday morning to Friday noon, and reach all three atolls, so the liveaboard converts a long day-boat run into unlimited access to Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe and Glover''s.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How deep is the Great Blue Hole dive and do you need to be certified?","a":"The dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft — at or beyond the recreational limit — to see the stalactites that hang between roughly 100–140 ft. Bottom time is measured in minutes and nitrogen narcosis is a real factor, so reputable operators strongly recommend or require Advanced Open Water certification. It is a deliberately deep dive, not a beginner novelty.","source":"dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is there to do on the Belize atolls if you don''t dive?","a":"The atoll cayes carry barefoot reef-island character for surface-interval and non-diver days. Tobacco Caye is a few-acre reef caye with snorkel-off-the-dock access; Half Moon Caye is a natural monument with ~4,000 nesting red-footed boobies and an observation tower; Long Caye is the inhabited base camp for Blue Hole and Half Moon Caye dives.","source":"belizeadventure.ca, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is it safe to dive the Belize atolls right now?","a":"Yes, with the standard disclosure. Belize is at US State Dept Level 3 (reissued June 18, 2026, code C/Crime only), but the only named-restricted zone is Southside Belize City — geographically disjoint from the offshore atolls. The liveaboard departs the Belize City marina and turns immediately for open water; guests transit rather than linger.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-06-18","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on an atoll dive trip?","a":"Offshore remoteness from the chamber. The only DAN-Preferred recompression chamber in Belize is on San Pedro, Ambergris Caye — hours of boat-then-air transit from a hit at Lighthouse Reef (~70 km/43 mi offshore) or Glover''s. Liveaboards carry onboard O2 and run DAN protocols as first response, which is why depth and deco discipline are non-negotiable and DAN insurance with evacuation coverage is effectively mandatory.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How long do you have to wait to fly after diving the Blue Hole?","a":"Plan an 18–24 hour buffer. DAN guidance sets a minimum 12-hour surface interval after a single no-deco dive and a minimum 18 hours after multi-day repetitive diving, which every liveaboard trip is; 24 hours is the recommended general practice. A 7-night Aggressor charter ends diving Friday around noon for a Saturday departure precisely to give that buffer before the BZE flight home.","source":"dan.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Great Blue Hole & Belize Atolls Diving — Liveaboard, Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe & Glover''s | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Belize Blue Hole liveaboard","diving Lighthouse Reef Belize","Belize Aggressor","Great Blue Hole dive depth","Turneffe Atoll diving","Glover''s Reef liveaboard","Half Moon Caye Wall dive","Belize whale shark diving Gladden Spit","no fly after diving Belize"],"hreflang":["en"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Private full-boat liveaboard charter (Belize Aggressor III/IV buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/belize"},{"name":"Turneffe Island Resort (luxury all-inclusive dive)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA) all-inclusive dive package","source":"https://visitturneffe.org/discover/where-to-stay-on-turneffe-atoll/"},{"name":"Gladden Private Island (adjacent, southern Belize)","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on channel","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.3158,"lng":-87.5346}}'::jsonb, 10),
  ('bocas-del-toro-panama', '10S', 'Bocas del Toro, Panama', 'Panama', 'Islands strung on a turquoise thread **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Panama', '{"tropical","diveglobal","romance","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_text":"Exercise Increased Caution (crime + potential civil unrest)","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"remote_flag":true,"hazards":["riptides (Red Frog)","advanced reef surf breaks (Bluff/Paunch)","water-taxi/boat transfers","dengue/zika/chikungunya","non-potable tap water (bottled only)"],"medical":"Bocas Town private clinic; Changuinola ~3h; Panama City evac ~11h road / short flight. Medical-evac insurance advised.","unrest_history":"State of emergency May-Jun 2025 (protests); lifted 2025-06-29; US personnel prohibition lifted 2025-07-08. Monitor before campaigns."},"timing":{"peak_windows":["Feb-Mar (driest + best viz + surf peak)","Sep-Oct (driest secondary + low crowds)"],"surf_peak":"Dec-Mar (secondary Jun-Jul)","inflection":"late Nov -> Dec","off_season_fill":["Nov (wettest)","Apr-May","Aug"],"fire_date":["~2026-01-18 (for Feb-Mar peak)","~2026-08-20 (for Sep-Oct peak)"],"note":"Caribbean-Panama inverts the national dry season; driest = Feb-Mar and Sep-Oct."},"jewels":[{"name":"Zapatilla Cays","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-tour referral + non-commissionable park fee","source":"https://go.bocasdeltoro.travel/destinations/cayos-zapatillas/","hook":"two uninhabited, reef-sheltered cays inside Bastimentos National Marine Park; postcard white sand + snorkeling","si":"tropical","blurb":"two uninhabited, reef-sheltered cays inside Bastimentos National Marine Park; postcard white sand + snorkeling","commission":"day-tour referral + non-commissionable park fee"},{"name":"Starfish Beach (Playa Estrella)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"island-hop boat-tour referral","source":"https://sallysees.com/beaches-in-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"shallow, glass-clear water full of starfish on Isla Colón''s northwest tip; the archipelago''s most photographed spot","si":"tropical","blurb":"shallow, glass-clear water full of starfish on Isla Colón''s northwest tip; the archipelago''s most photographed spot","commission":"island-hop boat-tour referral"},{"name":"Red Frog Beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Red Frog Beach resort booking + boat transfer","source":"https://www.redfrogbeach.com/about","si":"tropical","commission":"Red Frog Beach resort booking + boat transfer"},{"name":"Wizard Beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided walk / surf-school referral","source":"https://mokumsurfclub.com/ultimate-bocas-del-toro-guide/","si":"tropical","commission":"guided walk / surf-school referral"},{"name":"Cayo Coral (Coral Cay)","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"essential","commission_path":"dive/snorkel operator referral","source":"https://www.snorkeling-report.com/spot/snorkeling-cayo-coral-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"easy patch reef, 10–12 ft, mooring buoys, floating restaurants alongside. Ideal first-timer snorkel","si":"Dive/Snorkel","blurb":"easy patch reef, 10–12 ft, mooring buoys, floating restaurants alongside. Ideal first-timer snorkel","commission":"dive/snorkel operator referral"},{"name":"Bastimentos National Marine Park reefs","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"PADI operator package + park fee","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/outdoors-and-nature/nature-parks/national-parks/bastimentos-island/","si":"Dive/Snorkel","commission":"PADI operator package + park fee"},{"name":"Dolphin Bay","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"essential","commission_path":"boat-tour referral (ethical operators)","source":"https://bocastours.com/en/packages/zapatilla-cay-tour","hook":"resident dolphin pods; combines with Zapatilla day tours","si":"Dive/Snorkel","blurb":"resident dolphin pods; combines with Zapatilla day tours","commission":"boat-tour referral (ethical operators)"},{"name":"Bioluminescence night tour","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"guided night-tour referral","source":"https://azoravoyages.com/customize-my-trip/panama-all-tours/bocas-del-toro-activities-tours/","hook":"2-hr boat rides across dark bays where plankton light up on movement. Pure honeymoon set-piece","si":"romance","blurb":"2-hr boat rides across dark bays where plankton light up on movement. Pure honeymoon set-piece","commission":"guided night-tour referral"},{"name":"Overwater villa nights (Nayara)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","commission_path":"luxury AOR / bedbank / affiliate","source":"https://nayarabocasdeltoro.com/stay/","hook":"adults-only, plunge pools, glass-floor windows over the reef","si":"romance","blurb":"adults-only, plunge pools, glass-floor windows over the reef","commission":"luxury AOR / bedbank / affiliate"},{"name":"Oreba / Ngäbe cacao-farm tour","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"community-tour referral","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/places-to-visit/bocas-del-toro/things-to-do/culture-and-arts/indigenous-communities/","hook":"indigenous-guided walk through a working cacao farm + artisanal chocolate. Cultural moat + weather-tolerant","si":"expedition","blurb":"indigenous-guided walk through a working cacao farm + artisanal chocolate. Cultural moat + weather-tolerant","commission":"community-tour referral"},{"name":"Bahía Honda Timorogo aquatic-trail + bat cave","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"community-tour referral","source":"https://www.natureretreats.org/listing/ngobe-timorogo-community-ecotourism-project/","hook":"community ecotourism boat trail into a bat cave","si":"expedition","blurb":"community ecotourism boat trail into a bat cave","commission":"community-tour referral"},{"name":"Surf the Bluff / Paunch / Wizard","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"surf-school / lesson referral","source":"https://mokumsurfclub.com/ultimate-bocas-del-toro-guide/","hook":"Sharp split by ability: Bluff and Paunch are advanced reef breaks; Wizard is beginner-friendly when small and used by surf schools","si":"expedition","blurb":"Sharp split by ability: Bluff and Paunch are advanced reef breaks; Wizard is beginner-friendly when small and used by surf schools","commission":"surf-school / lesson referral"},{"name":"Bocas Town Caribbean nightlife","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"F&B / experience add-on (drives room-nights)","source":"https://www.takeyourbackpack.com/backpacking-in-panama/visit-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"the stilted harbor town''s bars, over-water clubs, and reggae/soca scene","si":"expedition","blurb":"the stilted harbor town''s bars, over-water clubs, and reggae/soca scene","commission":"F&B / experience add-on (drives room-nights)"}],"faq":null,"seo":{"meta_title":"Bocas del Toro, Panama Travel Guide 2026 — Islands, Reefs, Overwater Villas | TravelWell","search_language":"es-PA","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","local_keywords":["Bocas del Toro qué hacer","Cayos Zapatillas","Isla Bastimentos","Bocas del Toro cuándo ir","playa Estrella Bocas","surf en Bocas del Toro","tour bioluminiscencia Bocas","villas sobre el agua Panamá"],"hreflang":["en","es-PA"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Nayara Bocas del Toro","island":"Frangipani","model":"luxury-resort / Virtuoso-style preferred","tier":"luxury","mor":false,"note":"CNT #1 Central America; adults-only overwater"},{"name":"Sweet Bocas","model":"whole-estate MoR buyout","tier":"$$$$$","mor":true,"note":"AD-featured 9-BR teak overwater private-island villa; ~26 adults; $10,500/night base"},{"name":"Red Frog Beach Island Resort","island":"Bastimentos","model":"resort + villa commission","tier":"$$$","mor":"villa inventory via Red Frog Property"},{"name":"Isla Palenque","model":"luxury private-island (Pacific Gulf of Chiriquí — NOT Bocas)","tier":"luxury","mor":false,"note":"two-coast Panama add-on, not a Bocas jewel"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bocas del Toro, Panama, Panama"},"geo":{"lat":9.3402,"lng":-82.2417}}'::jsonb, 11),
  ('bogota-colombia', '10S', 'Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia', 'Colombia', 'Andean capital, paramo on its doorstep **TravelWell', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Bogotá & The Andes', '{"romance","adventure","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Bogotá sits at ~2,640 m (8,660 ft) — one of the highest capital cities on earth; expect mild soroche (altitude effects) for 24–48 hrs on arrival.","The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) holds ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, incl. the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend.","Monserrate rises to 3,152 m over the city, reached by funicular, cable car or a steep daytime walk, with the Basilica at the summit.","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral is a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine ~1.5–2 hrs from the city; Villa de Leyva has Colombia''s largest cobbled plaza (14,000 m²) and a Cretaceous fossil valley.","Bogotá''s driest, clearest windows are Dec–Mar and Jul–Aug; the biennial Ibero-American Theatre Festival returns August 2026."],"safety":{"emergency":"123","hospital":"Bogotá top private clinics (stabilization); serious cases route to US medical evacuation — evac-grade insurance advised","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"risk_code_meanings":{"C":"Crime — violent crime (murder, assault, robbery), drugging (scopolamine/''devil''s breath''), extortion, express kidnapping occur throughout Colombia incl. cities","T":"Terrorism — attacks possible with little/no warning; car bombs, grenades, IEDs, drones","U":"Unrest — demonstrations can shut roads and turn violent","K":"Kidnapping or Hostage-Taking — kidnapping-for-ransom reported","N":"Natural Disaster — earthquake, landslide (advisory names Bogotá for landslide risk)"},"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"bogota_in_named_danger":false,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Colombia (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"BOG (El Dorado Intl) — direct international incl. major US, EU and LatAm gateways; Colombia''s primary hub","altitude_m":2640,"altitude_note":"~2,640 m — mild AMS possible 24–48 hrs; Monserrate 3,152 m and páramo hikes 3,200 m+ add load","water":"Bogotá tap generally potable (meets WHO standards per EAAB/Ministry of Health); caveat aging plumbing in older buildings — bottled is conservative default","disease_note":"dengue LOW at altitude (vector scarce above ~1,800 m); rises for low-altitude excursions","scopolamine_caution":"''devil''s breath''/burundanga drugging — colourless/tasteless; Bogotá hotspot (1,409 cases 2023, Chapinero/Teusaquillo/Santa Fe); never accept drinks/food/tabs from strangers; dating-app method documented","personal_safety":"vetted taxi/ride-app only; no wealth display; zone discipline (La Candelaria daytime); do not resist a robbery"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec–Mar (dry, peak season) and Jul–Aug (dry + biennial Ibero-American Theatre Festival, even years)","inflection_curve_start":"early December (Christmas peak); August 2026 (Theatre Festival + dry season); Semana Santa (late Mar/early Apr)","fire_date":"mid-to-late November (Dec–Mar peak); ~mid-July (Aug festival/dry peak); ~early March (Semana Santa)","event_peaks":[{"event":"Ibero-American Theatre Festival","dates_2026":"August 2026 (biennial, even years)","note":"800+ productions from 40+ countries; stacks on dry season"},{"event":"Semana Santa (Holy Week)","dates":"late March / early April","note":"major domestic-travel pulse across the Andes"},{"event":"Christmas–New Year","dates":"Dec 20–Jan 6","note":"peak congestion + higher rates"}],"off_season_fill":"Apr–May and Oct–Nov (green/wetter shoulders, lower rates, thinner crowds)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gold Museum (Museo del Oro)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"city-tour affiliate; entry non-comm pass-through","source":"https://www.viator.com/Bogota-attractions/Gold-Museum/d4560-a6188","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend; free on Sundays","si":"culture","blurb":"~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend; free on Sundays","when":"year-round","commission":"city-tour affiliate; entry non-comm pass-through"},{"name":"Botero Museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"city-tour affiliate; free entry","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Fernando Botero''s donated collection, free entry, in La Candelaria","si":"culture","blurb":"Fernando Botero''s donated collection, free entry, in La Candelaria","when":"year-round","commission":"city-tour affiliate; free entry"},{"name":"La Candelaria colonial core + street art","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"walking-tour affiliate + boutique lodging","source":"https://kittiaroundtheworld.com/things-to-do-in-la-candelaria-bogota-historic-centre/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Plaza de Bolívar, 17th-c. Iglesia de Santa Clara, mural-covered lanes, the number-one neighbourhood in the city","si":"culture","blurb":"Plaza de Bolívar, 17th-c. Iglesia de Santa Clara, mural-covered lanes, the number-one neighbourhood in the city","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"walking-tour affiliate + boutique lodging"},{"name":"Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-trip DMC/operator; entry non-comm pass-through","source":"https://thecolombianway.com/en/our-trips/day-trips/the-salt-cathedral-of-zipaquira/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine, glowing tunnels, carved crosses, an underground dome; ~1.5–2 hrs from Bogotá","si":"culture","blurb":"a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine, glowing tunnels, carved crosses, an underground dome; ~1.5–2 hrs from Bogotá","when":"year-round","commission":"day-trip DMC/operator; entry non-comm pass-through"},{"name":"Villa de Leyva (colonial plaza + fossils)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","commission_path":"overnight DMC + colonial-house/finca villa MoR","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_de_Leyva","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a whitewashed-town weekend around the great plaza, star-filled Andean skies, boutique fincas — the plateau''s romance run","si":"culture","blurb":"a whitewashed-town weekend around the great plaza, star-filled Andean skies, boutique fincas — the plateau''s romance run","when":"year-round","commission":"overnight DMC + colonial-house/finca villa MoR"},{"name":"Monserrate sunset (funicular/cable car)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","commission_path":"hotel + funicular non-comm + DMC dining","source":"https://kittiaroundtheworld.com/things-to-do-in-la-candelaria-bogota-historic-centre/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"hotel + funicular non-comm + DMC dining"},{"name":"Usaquén Sunday market + brunch","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","commission_path":"boutique-lodging + food-tour affiliate","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g294074-d1382992-Reviews-Mercado_de_las_Pulgas_de_Usaquen-Bogota.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the colonial northern district; every Sunday ~10:00–18:00 the streets fill with artisans, antiques, Colombian coffee and long brunches around the plaza","si":"romance","blurb":"the colonial northern district; every Sunday ~10:00–18:00 the streets fill with artisans, antiques, Colombian coffee and long brunches around the plaza","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"boutique-lodging + food-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Chingaza páramo hike","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","commission_path":"GEA DMC / licensed guide + park permit","source":"https://mytriptocolombia.com/hiking-chingaza-national-park-travel-guide/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a magnificent páramo on Bogotá''s outskirts, frailejón moorland, glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, guided day trips from the city","si":"adventure","blurb":"a magnificent páramo on Bogotá''s outskirts, frailejón moorland, glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, guided day trips from the city","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide + park permit"},{"name":"Suesca rock-climbing","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"essential","commission_path":"adventure DMC / climbing-school affiliate","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/colombia/day-trips-weekend-breaks-from-bogota-2019/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Colombia''s best climbing crag, ~1 hr north; sandstone canyon walls, beginner-to-advanced routes through local climbing schools","si":"adventure","blurb":"Colombia''s best climbing crag, ~1 hr north; sandstone canyon walls, beginner-to-advanced routes through local climbing schools","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"adventure DMC / climbing-school affiliate"},{"name":"Sumapaz páramo trek","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","commission_path":"GEA DMC / licensed guide (guided-only)","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/day-hikes-bogota-colombia","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","si":"adventure","blurb":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide (guided-only)"},{"name":"Paloquemao market + coffee","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"food-tour affiliate + DMC","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","si":"culinary","blurb":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"food-tour affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Andrés Carne de Res (Chía)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC dining + vetted transport","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g815502-d939879-Reviews-Andres_Carne_De_Res_Chia-Chia_Cundinamarca_Department.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","si":"culinary","blurb":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"DMC dining + vetted transport"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the most romantic thing to do in Bogotá?","a":"Ride the funicular or cable car up Monserrate at dusk for dinner at the summit restaurant, with the whole plateau of light beneath you — the city''s signature romance run. The ridge rises to 3,152 m (10,341 ft), and the Basilica crowns the summit.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you go hiking near Bogotá?","a":"Yes — Andean páramo day-hikes start on the city''s doorstep and run guided. Chingaza páramo climbs from 2,600 to 4,000 m through frailejón moorland and glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, while Suesca, about 1 hour north, is Colombia''s premier rock-climbing crag. Guided entry is the norm for the páramos.","source":"mytriptocolombia.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"What are the must-see museums and sights in Bogotá?","a":"The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) is the headline — ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, including the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend, and free on Sundays — alongside the Botero Museum and colonial La Candelaria. The core clusters in and above the historic centre.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Where should you eat and drink around Bogotá?","a":"Andrés Carne de Res in Chía is the marquee night out — ranked #2 of 139 restaurants in Chía, a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors, about 40–60 min north of the city. In town, Zona G is Bogotá''s dense \"gourmet zone.\"","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Is Bogotá safe to visit right now?","a":"Colombia sits at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (issued 2026-03-31, codes C·T·U·K·N), but Bogotá (Cundinamarca) is NOT among the named Level-4 Do-Not-Travel areas — those are Arauca, Cauca (excl. Popayán), Valle del Cauca (excl. Cali), Norte de Santander, and within ~10 km of the Venezuela border. Bogotá has direct international air (BOG).","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bogotá?","a":"Scopolamine (\"devil''s breath\" / burundanga) drugging is the headline traveler risk — a colourless, tasteless sedative used to rob or assault. Bogotá police recorded 1,409 cases in 2023 (+16% year-on-year), concentrated in Chapinero, Teusaquillo and Santa Fe, often via dating apps and offered drinks. Never accept drinks or tabs from strangers.","source":"thecitypaperbogota.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is walking up Monserrate dangerous?","a":"Walk the Monserrate pilgrimage trail only in daylight and in groups — robberies have been reported on the path — or take the funicular or cable car instead. The summit stands at 3,152 m, so pace yourself for the altitude.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia — Gold Museum, Monserrate, Zipaquirá & Villa de Leyva | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CO","long_tail_en":["things to do in Bogotá Colombia","Gold Museum Bogotá guide","Monserrate funicular Bogotá","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral day trip from Bogotá","Villa de Leyva from Bogotá","is Bogotá safe 2026","Bogotá altitude sickness"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Bogotá","Catedral de Sal Zipaquirá","Museo del Oro","Villa de Leyva","Monserrate Bogotá","hoteles de lujo Bogotá"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","adventure","culture","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Casa Medina","type":"landmark 1946 building, Zona G, 62 rooms + 19 suites, Ministry-of-Culture monument","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Bogotá","type":"second FS property, Zona T entertainment district, contemporary tower","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Sofitel Bogotá Victoria Regia","type":"French-luxury prestige address, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury→ultra"},{"name":"W Bogotá (Zona T)","type":"Marriott lifestyle-luxury flagship, design-forward rooftop","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Click Clack Hotel","type":"design-forward boutique, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"premium→luxury"},{"name":"Zona G / Chicó luxury-apartment buyouts","type":"serviced multi-bedroom apartments w/ concierge","routing":"MoR villa + host","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":4.711,"lng":-74.0721}}'::jsonb, 12)
